{"type":"assistant/message","seq":605,"time":1793893205541,"data":{"turn":4,"step":22,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"Old `--rail` tokens remain but unused. Could remove. They don't affect. Clean up for quality:\n- Remove lines 44-47 and 83-85 (rail tokens). Also `--rail-ink`, etc. No usage. Do it.\n- `.sidebar-rail` is new. Fine.\n\nNow we need to verify the visual layout by reading CSS around sidebar and comparing to HTML. Potential issues:\n\n1. **CSS `.sb-brand`**: the brand anchor is inside `.sb-top`; `.sb-top` height 44, brand + toggle. Good.\n2. **Sidebar width 288**: `.sidebar` has padding 6 8; content width 272. `.sb-sessions` etc. Good.\n3. **Nav item active**: background surface; on paper-2. Good.\n4. **Session list**: active background surface; good.\n5. **Sidebar collapsed**: width 56 from grid; `.sidebar` padding 6 0; align-items center; children 36. Good.\n6. **Account menu**: z-index 95; but sidebar has z-index 20; stacking context? `.sidebar` has `position:relative; z-index:20` creating a stacking context, so the account menu's z-index 95 is within the sidebar's stacking context (z 20). The menu will be above chat? Chat has no z-index. Sidebar context z 20 > chat. So menu visible. Good. But trace z 20? Trace no z-index in base, but in fixed drawer z 60. On desktop trace in grid, no z-index; stacking order after sidebar/chat, but account menu fixed could be under trace if trace overlaps? The account menu is at left 64 bottom, trace at right. No overlap. Fine.\n7. **Sidebar collapsed account menu**: fixed within stacking context z 20; chat no z; visible. Good.\n8. **Mobile sidebar**: z 80, scrim 75. The account menu inside sidebar z 95 within sidebar context, above sidebar content. Good.\n9. **Mobile menu button**: chat header; no z. Scrim z75 covers. Good.\n10. **Trace fixed z60**: below scrim/sidebar. Good.\n11. **Desktop trace toggle**: unchanged.\n12. **Sidebar collapsed**: `.app.sidebar-collapsed` grid 56. The sidebar `overflow:hidden` and padding. Good.\n13. **Sidebar expanded to collapsed transition**: grid-template-columns transitions; content instantly switches (sb-sessions display none, brand hidden). No fade. Acceptable for prototype. DSH has fancy animation; user asked style, not exact animation. Could add a subtle transition on opacity for `.sb-brand`, `.sb-sessions`, etc. Not necessary.\n14. **Sidebar collapse button position**: In expanded, toggle is at right of brand. In collapsed, only toggle centered. Good.\n15. **Account menu collapsed**: fixed left 64. Good.\n16. **Account menu expanded**: absolute left 8 right 8 bottom 62. Good.\n17. **Account menu on mobile**: absolute inside fixed sidebar. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **`.sidebar` z-index 20** and **`.account-menu` fixed** when collapsed: the stack context z20 is above chat, so menu visible. Good.\n- The scrim z75 when mobile; sidebar z80. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **`.sb-sessions` flex:1 but no `overflow:hidden`**. `.session-scroll` has overflow auto and flex 1. The parent `.sb-sessions` min-height 0. Good.\n- `.sb-sessions` contains head, search, scroll. The search margin. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **`.search` global** may apply to any other search in the page? Only one. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **`.session-scroll`** has padding 0 2px 8px. Sessions. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **`sb-sessions-head h2`** is 11px; \"会话\" label. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **`sb-sessions-head .mono` count 7**; good.\n\nPotential issue: **`.sb-conn` 3 ONLINE**; good.\n\nPotential issue: **account sub \"3 个智能体在线\"**; good.\n\nPotential issue: **`sb-account` collapsed 36x36**, avatar 30; good.\n\nPotential issue: **account menu items 33px**; total height; good.\n\nPotential issue: **the theme icon swap** in the menu: both icons are inside the button; `.ic-sun` display none default, `.ic-moon` block. In dark, sun block, moon none. Good.\n- But the `.menu-item` `gap:8px` and two icons: hidden one still `display:none`, fine.\n\nPotential issue: **the theme toggle listener** uses `showToast`; menu closes via listener. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **The account menu \"设置\" item** has data-demo; click shows toast and closes menu and mobile drawer. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **The account menu \"账号\" item** has data-demo. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **The account menu \"退出登录\"** has data-demo. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **The account menu lacks a divider between account and settings?** It has head, sep, account, settings, theme, sep, logout, version. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **The sidebar brand is an `<a href=\"#\">`**; clicking it may scroll to top. No issue.\n\nPotential issue: **The mobile sidebar button is hidden on desktop** via display none, but the `.chat-head` gap still applies? Hidden elements don't participate. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **The chat-heading flex:1** added. On desktop, heading takes available space; actions right. Good.\n- With `justify-content:space-between`, heading flex 1 plus actions. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: **At ≤760, `.chat-actions .status-chip` hidden; chat-actions has panel icon.** Good.\n- The mobile menu button remains at left. Good.\n- Title and panel icon. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: **At ≤900, the sidebar is fixed and hides by transform; the app chat full width. The sidebar toggle inside is unavailable when closed; the mobile button in header opens.** Good.\n- The mobile button `aria-expanded` false. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **`narrowSidebar` change event**: when crossing from desktop to mobile, if the account menu is open (fixed), `setAccountMenu(false)` closes. Good.\n- It removes `sidebar-open` (already false). It removes `sidebar-collapsed`. Good.\n- When crossing back to desktop, `sidebarToggle` aria set based on collapsed (false after removal → true). Good.\n- Mobile button aria false. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **Initial mobile**: `if (narrowSidebar.matches) { app.classList.remove('sidebar-collapsed'); sidebarToggle.setAttribute('aria-expanded','false'); }`. Good.\n- But the `sidebarToggle` HTML aria initially true; set false. Good.\n- The mobile button initial aria false. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **Initial desktop**: no class, toggle aria true. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **Desktop collapsed then reload**: no persistence. Not required. Could persist in localStorage. User didn't ask. DSH may persist. Not necessary.\n\nPotential issue: **Mobile drawer closes on session click**: `setMobileSidebar(false)` defined before session block. Good.\n- The session click also updates active. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **Mobile drawer closes on new session**: added. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **Mobile drawer closes on nav data-demo**: added. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **Escape closes mobile drawer**: added. Good.\n\nPotential issue: **Clicking scrim closes**: added.\n\nPotential issue: **Focus trap**: not implemented. Prototype. Fine.\n\nNow **restored feature cards**:\n- `.kind-skill` and `.kind-mcp` CSS restored. But the `.kind-skill .tool-card` selector requires the card to be a descendant of `.kind-skill` li. Yes.\n- The `.kind-mcp .node` purple. Good.\n- The MCP card body `.mcp-line`, `.kv` restored.\n- The skill card body `.proc-desc`, `.chips`, `.chip` restored.\n- The tool card `.kind-tool` existing. Good.\n- The `.hit` styles for tool card still exist. Good.\n- The user bubble attachment `.attach` styles. Good.\n- The composer attachment button. Good.\n\n**Check the tool card and skill card order in thread**. Read a bit. Use grep. Also check the MCP card. We'll inspect.\n\n**Check CSS `.kind-skill` etc. insertion** before reduced-motion. Good.\n\n**Check `--mcp` tokens**. Good.\n\n**Check `.trace` 7 steps**. Good.\n\n**Check `.agents` 3**. Good.\n\n**Check `sb-conn` 3**. Good.\n\n**Check session count 7**. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: the A2A group footer / thread footer**:\n- A2A group foot: `2 A2A tasks / 2 artifacts / A2A 1.0`. Good.\n- Thread foot: `2 done / 1 awaiting approval`. But now there are more tasks (skill, tools, MCP). \"2 done\" refers A2A. It's ambiguous. Could change to `A2A 2 done / 1 awaiting approval`. Or `2 A2A done / 1 awaiting`. The current text was from v3. To avoid confusion, change to `A2A 2 done / Slack 1 awaiting`. Hmm.\n- Since the thread foot is a small summary, use `2 A2A done / 1 MCP awaiting`. Or `2 done / 1 awaiting approval` is okay. I'd update to `2 A2A done / 1 awaiting approval`. This is more accurate.\n- Do it.\n\n**Potential issue: the right trace header count 7** and steps 7. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: the top header sub \"待审批\"**; the status chip \"待审批\". Good.\n\n**Potential issue: the session first item \"待审批\"**. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: the account \"3 ONLINE\"** and 3 agents. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: the `publisher-agent` removed**; approval uses Slack MCP. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: `fact-checker` removed**; A2A data/editorial. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: the intro mentions \"data-analyst\" and \"editorial-reviewer\"**. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: the A2A group row tags `skill · verify_numbers` and `skill · review_copy`**. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: the approval risk row \"执行方 slack-mcp · streamable-http\"** and MCP card. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: the MCP card appears after A2A; approval after MCP. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: the approval action says \"通过 Slack MCP 把周报发布\". Good.\n\n**Potential issue: the approval's \"目标 #support-weekly · 12 名成员\" matches MCP card. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: the approval's \"副作用 24 小时内可撤回\"**; Slack messages can be edited/deleted within some time? Not a strict API. It's a product statement. Fine.\n\n**Potential issue: the HITL run is waiting; top status \"待审批\"; send disabled. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: approve 1.8s later marks track last step done; but the MCP step before is done. Good.\n- `updateTrackOutcome` targets `.track li:last-child`; there is one track. Good.\n- It sets time 0.4s. Good.\n- The approval card resolved text \"Slack 消息已发布.\" Good.\n- Token label \"本轮\". Good.\n- Top status \"已完成\". Good.\n\n**Potential issue: reject marks track sub \"已取消 · Slack 发送\"; top status \"已取消\"; approval card red. Good. The track last item remains is-wait (dashed), sub canceled. Fine.\n\n**Potential issue: approve/resolved-note color** green; reject red. CSS from v3. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: `approvalCard.classList.add('is-resolved')` and `is-rejected`; CSS `.approval-card.is-rejected` overrides green. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: `approvalStatus` after reject class status-chip (gray). Good.\n\n**Potential issue: `runStatus` after approve completion `is-ok`; dot `is-ok`; text \"已完成\". Good.\n\n**Potential issue: `runStatus` after reject `status-chip`; dot plain; text \"已取消\". Good.\n\nNow remove unused `--rail` tokens. Change thread foot text. Maybe adjust `.sb-new` hover etc.\n\nAlso **the sidebar account menu \"设置\"** is a data-demo, so clicking it doesn't navigate to a settings page. The user asked \"点击弹出可选择\" — menu item exists; prototype toast. Fine.\n\n**Potential issue: The settings page no longer in nav; no standalone settings page. The account menu item is the entry. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: The user might expect \"左侧栏可收起\" with a visible expand button when collapsed. The toggle remains at top of 56px rail. Good.\n- The rail's toggle icon is `i-panel` (panel-left outline). When collapsed, it still looks like panel; clicking expands. Fine.\n- Could rotate/change icon to indicate expand. Not necessary.\n\n**Potential issue: The sidebar collapsed rail still shows brand? No, hidden. DSH rail often shows logo at top. Our collapsed rail shows only toggle, new, nav, avatar. The brand mark is hidden. Maybe should show logo instead of toggle? DSH rail shows whale logo and toggle? Let's check DSH: `logoRow` with brand and toggle. In collapsed, `.root.collapsed` padding; brand might remain? The CSS `.root.collapsed` and `logoRow` maybe shows logo. The DSH rail has a whale logo at top and toggle. For our design, collapsed rail with only toggle at top is functional but less branded.\n- Could show brand mark in collapsed state: `.sidebar-collapsed .sb-brand{display:flex}` but hide the text. That would put logo + toggle? The `.sb-top` has brand + toggle; collapsed width 56 can't fit both side by side. Could stack? DSH rail shows logo and toggle maybe in separate rows.\n- Simpler: in collapsed state, show the brand mark instead of the toggle? But then how to expand? Clicking logo could expand. Hmm.\n- Current: top has toggle only; brand hidden. The new button below has plus; nav icons. The rail is functional. Brand identity lost when collapsed. Acceptable.\n- Could put the brand mark above the toggle (two rows) in collapsed: `.sb-top{flex-direction:column;height:auto;gap:4px}` with brand shown as mark only and toggle. That takes 2*28+gap = 60. Then new, nav. Might be nice.\n  - CSS: `.app.sidebar-collapsed .sb-top{flex-direction:column;height:auto;gap:4px;padding:0}`; `.sidebar-collapsed .sb-brand{display:flex}`; `.sidebar-collapsed .sb-brand span{display:none}`; brand width 28 height 28; mark 22. Toggle below. This gives logo + toggle.\n  - DSH rail likely shows logo + toggle? The rail spec says \"18px from the rail top to the whale's box (24px to the 24-wide whale glyph itself)\" and toggle is in topStrip fixed. In collapsed, logoRow height 0 for Windows; for macOS maybe. Hmm.\n  - Our simplified rail: toggle at top, then new, nav, avatar. It's okay.\n  - User asked DSH style; the brand being hidden when collapsed is a minor difference. Could show brand mark at top and toggle below. Let's consider height: 56 width, top 44. If brand + toggle stacked, 22+28+gap = 54, exceeding 44; set height auto. Then new. Total top 58 + new 50 + nav 4*38=152 + avatar 42 = 302. Fine at 900.\n  - Visual: logo at top center, toggle below. But the toggle icon is small; could be confused.\n  - Alternative: make the brand mark itself the expand button when collapsed. Complex.\n  - Keep current; the user can see DSH-style via the expanded sidebar and rail collapse. The requirement is collapse, not brand in rail. Fine.\n\n**Potential issue: The sidebar toggle at expanded is on the far right of the brand row, DSH-like. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: The sidebar has no top margin/brand spacing? `.sb-top` padding 0 2 0 6, height 44. Fine.\n\n**Potential issue: the sidebar's background paper-2 and chat paper. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: the account menu uses `--shadow-md`, border. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: the sidebar footer account row is at the very bottom with padding 6 8. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: The connection status line above account. Good.\n\n**Potential issue: The session list may push the footer; flex. Good.\n\nNow remove unused `--rail` tokens and change footer text.\n\nAlso, **the composer attachment button**: restored before \"智能体\". Good.\n\n**The composer \"附件\" data-demo** will show toast. Good.\n\n**The user message attachment chip** in dark bubble. `.prompt-bubble .attach` styles. Good.\n\n**The attachment `.attach` style** uses `background:var(--surface)` base, but in bubble override. Good.\n\n**The `attachments` margin-top 10/11. Good.\n\nNow check if the **MCP card** is too tall; okay.\n\n**Check if `.kind-skill`/`.kind-mcp` CSS appears after `.kind` and before media. Good.\n\n**Check if `.mcp-line` etc. are not duplicated. Fine.\n\n**Check `.chips` etc. not conflicting with other `.chip` uses. Only skill. Fine.\n\n**Check `.kv` global may conflict with anything? Only MCP. Fine.\n\nNow add the `--rail` cleanup and footer text. Also maybe remove `--rail` tokens from both root/dark. Do it.\n\nThread foot current: `2 done / 1 awaiting approval`. Change to `2 A2A done / 1 awaiting approval`. Good.\n\n**One more thing**: The top chat-sub currently \"main-agent / 待审批 / run_9a8b7c\". The status chip \"待审批\". Good.\n\n**One more thing**: The session list count 7, yes.\n\n**One more thing**: The account menu \"个人工作区\" and \"Agent Hub v0.1.0\". Fine.\n\n**One more thing**: `rail-version` removed. Version in account menu and menu version. Good.\n\n**One more thing**: The old `.rail` tokens unused; remove.\n\nLet's patch."},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_CNTCPluTq0Ig3mEhHLUM7530","name":"bash","arguments":"{\"command\": \"cd /home/zhaodan/work/NodeJsProjects/agent-hub-web/docs/prototypes && python3 - <<'PY'\\npath='ui-v4.html'\\ns=open(path,encoding='utf-8').read()\\n\\ndef rep(old,new,count=1):\\n    global s\\n    assert old in s, 'MISSING: '+old[:100]\\n    s=s.replace(old,new,count)\\n\\n# remove unused dark-rail tokens\\nrep('''  --rail:#13191D;\\n  --rail-ink:#E8E7DE;\\n  --rail-muted:#8C979D;\\n  --rail-line:rgba(255,255,255,.09);\\n\\n''','')\\nrep('''  --rail:#080C0F;\\n  --rail-ink:#E8E7DF;\\n  --rail-muted:#849097;\\n\\n''','')\\n\\nrep('<span class=\\\"mono\\\">2 done / 1 awaiting approval</span>',\\n    '<span class=\\\"mono\\\">2 A2A done / 1 awaiting approval</span>')\\n\\nopen(path,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\\nprint('cleanup done')\\nPY\\npython3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom html.parser import HTMLParser\\nimport re, collections\\nsrc=open('ui-v4.html',encoding='utf-8').read()\\nVOID={'area','base','br','col','embed','hr','img','input','link','meta','param','source','track','wbr','path','circle','rect','line','polyline','polygon','ellipse','use','stop'}\\nclass P(HTMLParser):\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        super().__init__(convert_charrefs=True); self.stack=[]; self.err=[]; self.ids=[]\\n    def handle_starttag(self,t,a):\\n        d=dict(a)\\n        if 'id' in d:self.ids.append(d['id'])\\n        if t not in VOID:self.stack.append((t,self.getpos()))\\n    def handle_startendtag(self,t,a):\\n        d=dict(a)\\n        if 'id' in d:self.ids.append(d['id'])\\n    def handle_endtag(self,t):\\n        if t in VOID:return\\n        if not self.stack:self.err.append(('extra',t,self.getpos()));return\\n        if self.stack[-1][0]==t:self.stack.pop()\\n        else:self.err.append(('mismatch',t,self.getpos(),self.stack[-3:]))\\np=P();p.feed(src)\\nprint('tag errors:',p.err or 'none')\\nprint('unclosed:',p.stack or 'none')\\nprint('dup ids:',[k for k,v in collections.Counter(p.ids).items() if v>1] or 'none')\\ncss=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',src,re.S).group(1)\\nprint('css braces:',css.count('{'),css.count('}'))\\nopen('/tmp/proto4.js','w',encoding='utf-8').write(re.search(r'<script>(.*?)</script>',src,re.S).group(1))\\nprint('themeToggle count:', src.count('id=\\\"themeToggle\\\"'))\\nprint('sidebarTool id:', src.count('id=\\\"sidebarToggle\\\"'))\\nPY\\nnode --check /tmp/proto4.js && echo \\\"JS syntax OK\\\"; wc -l ui-v4.html; ls -lh ui-v4.html\", \"description\": \"Clean rail tokens and validate final structure\"}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-flash","replayState":{"response":{"kind":"deepseek-messages","version":1,"model":"deepseek-flash"},"blocks":[{"type":"reasoning","signature":"2958f2a9-5799-4571-bc93-1c61dd0d9f2c"},{"type":"tool-call"}]}},"id":"8e0c9bff-40e5-4755-bf6a-4522c6479d73"},"usage":{"inputTokens":515,"outputTokens":4886,"cacheReadTokens":360320,"cacheWriteTokens":0,"totalTokens":365721},"stream":[{"type":"chunk","time":1793893180221,"chunk":{"type":"block-start","index":0,"blockType":"reasoning"}},{"type":"reasoning-chunks","time0":1793893181260,"index":0,"dt":[164,18,0,0,12,0,17,0,0,0,31,1,0,0,0,0,14,1,0,0,16,17,0,0,18,0,0,10,1,0,14,0,76,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,11,1,0,0,18,0,0,0,0,13,1,0,0,16,15,0,0,18,45,0,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,34,15,1,0,12,0,0,13,0,18,1,0,0,0,0,16,0,12,0,18,1,14,19,11,1,16,0,0,0,0,17,0,0,0,13,0,0,0,15,16,15,0,1,0,0,0,19,0,0,16,0,11,0,0,20,0,14,1,0,0,14,1,0,19,10,1,0,0,0,14,16,0,0,14,0,0,0,0,0,15,17,15,0,21,10,0,0,17,13,0,0,18,0,0,0,0,0,14,17,0,0,15,1,0,15,0,1,0,0,14,0,16,0,16,0,0,22,0,0,0,7,1,0,0,14,0,0,0,0,25,0,0,0,0,27,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,11,1,30,0,0,4,1,10,0,0,18,0,0,0,0,14,1,15,1,0,0,0,17,1,0,0,15,0,0,0,0,0,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,1,0,0,0,12,0,0,0,0,0,21,0,0,0,0,8,0,0,0,24,7,19,0,0,13,18,0,13,0,0,0,32,0,0,14,0,0,0,15,0,0,15,0,17,1,0,0,2