{"type":"assistant/message","seq":700,"time":1793893762005,"data":{"turn":5,"step":1,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"The user wants:\n1. Sidebar sessions support right-click or more-actions, and session deletion.\n2. Provide sample pages for the other pages: 智能体、任务、知识库、设置 (and maybe login? \"其他几个页面\" likely the nav pages: 智能体、任务、知识库、设置). Need to create HTML samples for the other pages. Should they be in one file with navigation? The current prototype is a single chat page. The user wants \"其他几个页面的样例\" — likely separate page samples or one multi-page prototype. Best: create a single `ui-v4-pages.html` with a shared sidebar and multiple page views (smart agents, tasks, knowledge, settings) navigable via sidebar, plus maybe login? The nav has 对话、智能体、任务、知识库; settings via account menu. So the other pages are 智能体、任务、知识库、设置. Maybe also login/register (M1) not in nav. The user says \"其他几个页面\" — likely the four.\n\nWe need to decide whether to update v4 chat page with session context menu/delete, and create a separate multi-page sample file. Perhaps:\n- Update `ui-v4.html` (chat page) to add session more menu and delete.\n- Create `ui-v4-pages.html` with the same shell and four page views (Agents, Tasks, Knowledge, Settings), using the same DSH sidebar. It could be a separate file with internal page switching (data-page views) to show all samples in one file. That avoids duplicating the shell four times and makes it easy to review. Use JS to switch views and nav active state; hash maybe. The sidebar session list remains; clicking a session returns to chat? But the chat page is in ui-v4.html. If pages file is separate, clicking \"对话\" could link to ui-v4.html. \"智能体/任务/知识库\" switch internal views. Settings via account menu opens settings view. That seems good.\n- Alternatively, create four separate HTML files. The user said \"其他几个页面的样例\" (samples), one file with tabs is easier. But \"页面\" could mean separate pages. A single file with view 