 menu"," items","'"," text"," color",";"," fine",".\n","-"," The"," `.","menu","-se","p","`"," margin","."," Good",".\n","-"," The"," menu","'s"," `.","menu","-item","`"," has"," `","width",":","100","%","`",";"," good",".\n","-"," The"," `.","session","-menu","`"," is"," display"," none",";"," `.","is","-open","`"," block",".\n","-"," The"," `.","dialog","`"," has"," no"," max","-height",";"," fine",".\n\n","Add"," JS",".\n\n","Let","'s"," do"," the"," HTML","/C","SS"," first","."]},{"type":"chunk","time":1793893782621,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":0,"block":{"type":"reasoning","text":"Need verify the nav anchors closing tags replaced correctly. The loop searched for `</button>` after the new anchor; there might be an SVG `</svg>` etc. The first `</button>` after the anchor is the nav item's closing. Good. We should inspect the nav block.\n\nAlso add session menu/dialog HTML before toast. Find the toast block. Add:\n```html\n<div class=\"session-menu\" id=\"sessionMenu\" role=\"menu\" aria-label=\"会话操作\">\n  <button class=\"menu-item\" role=\"menuitem\" data-session-action=\"rename\">...重命名</button>\n  <button class=\"menu-item\" role=\"menuitem\" data-session-action=\"archive\">...归档</button>\n  <div class=\"menu-sep\"></div>\n  <button class=\"menu-item is-danger\" role=\"menuitem\" data-session-action=\"delete\">...删除会话</button>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"dialog-backdrop\" id=\"deleteDialog\">\n  <div class=\"dialog\" role=\"dialog\" aria-modal=\"true\" aria-labelledby=\"deleteTitle\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n    <h2 id=\"deleteTitle\">删除会话？</h2>\n    <p>“<span id=\"deleteSessionName\"></span>”及其消息将被删除，此操作不可撤销。</p>\n    <div class=\"dialog-actions\">\n      <button class=\"btn btn-outline\" id=\"cancelDelete\">取消</button>\n      <button class=\"btn btn-danger\" id=\"confirmDelete\">删除会话</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n- The `.menu-item` base in v4 has `.menu-item` styles; the session menu uses it. Good.\n- The menu `role=menu`; items.\n- The dialog backdrop no `aria-hidden`. Fine.\n- The dialog `tabindex=-1`.\n- The `deleteSessionName` span.\n- Add before toast.\n\nIcons: `i-edit`, `i-archive` (exists), `i-trash` (need add). Add symbols:\n- `i-edit`: `<path d=\"M4 20h4l10-10a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4-4L4 16v4Z\"/><path d=\"M13.5 6.5l4 4\"/>`\n- `i-trash`: `<path d=\"M4 7h16M9 7V4h6v3M7 7l1 13h8l1-13M10 11v6M14 11v6\"/>`\n- `i-archive` exists (box with line).\n- Use `.ic`.\n\nAdd menu items with icons:\n```html\n<button class=\"menu-item\" role=\"menuitem\" data-session-action=\"rename\">\n  <svg class=\"ic\"><use href=\"#i-edit\"/></svg>重命名\n</button>\n<button ... archive>...归档</button>\n<div class=\"menu-sep\"></div>\n<button class=\"menu-item is-danger\" ... delete>...删除会话</button>\n```\n- The `.menu-sep` CSS exists (account menu). The session menu uses. Good.\n\nAdd JS:\n- Vars after `var narrowSidebar...`:\n  `var sessionMenu = ...; var sessionMenuTarget = null; var sessionMenuAnchor = null; var deleteDialog = ...; var deleteSessionName = ...; var deleteSessionTarget = null; var sessionCount = ...;`\n- Wrap sessions after `var sessions = ...;` and before the click loop.\n- The more button icon.\n- The contextmenu.\n- Functions.\n- Search filter row.\n- Document listeners.\n- Rename.\n\nLet's carefully implement JS.\n\nCurrent v4/v5 JS session block:\n```js\n  /* ---------- session list ---------- */\n  var sessions = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.session'));\n  sessions.forEach(function (item) {\n    item.addEventListener('click', function () {\n      sessions.forEach(function (s) { ... });\n      item.classList.add('is-active');\n      item.setAttribute('aria-current', 'page');\n      if (narrowSidebar.matches) setMobileSidebar(false);\n    });\n  });\n\n  document.getElementById('newSession').addEventListener('click', ...);\n\n  var search = document.getElementById('sessionSearch');\n  search.addEventListener('input', function () {\n    var q = ...\n    var groups = ...\n    sessions.forEach(function (item) {\n      var title = ...\n      item.hidden = ...\n    });\n    groups.forEach(... !s.hidden ...);\n  });\n```\n- Insert wrapping after `var sessions = ...`:\n```js\n  sessions.forEach(function (item) {\n    var row = document.createElement('div');\n    row.className = 'session-row';\n    item.parentNode.insertBefore(row, item);\n    row.appendChild(item);\n    var more = document.createElement('button');\n    more.type = 'button';\n    more.className = 'session-more';\n    more.setAttribute('aria-label', '会话操作');\n    more.setAttribute('aria-haspopup', 'menu');\n    more.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');\n    more.title = '会话操作';\n    more.innerHTML = '<svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-more\"/></svg>';\n    row.appendChild(more);\n    more.addEventListener('click', function (event) {\n      event.stopPropagation();\n      openSessionMenu(row, more);\n    });\n    row.addEventListener('contextmenu', function (event) {\n      event.preventDefault();\n      openSessionMenu(row, null, event.clientX, event.clientY);\n    });\n  });\n```\n- The more button is inside row; the session button is also. The session button width 100%; the more overlays; the padding-right 30 to avoid text under. Good.\n- The row's context menu anywhere (including the session button). Good.\n- After wrapping, the active click listener still on item. The more button click doesn't bubble to the session button (sibling), so no selection; good.\n- The more button click stops propagation to document (so menu stays); good.\n- The row contextmenu doesn't select; fine.\n\n- Search filter:\n```js\n    sessions.forEach(function (item) {\n      var title = ...\n      var match = q === '' || title.indexOf(q) !== -1;\n      item.hidden = !match;\n      var row = item.closest('.session-row');\n      if (row) row.hidden = !match;\n    });\n```\n- The group visibility check uses `!s.hidden`; since item.hidden set, fine. But the group may have a row hidden and session hidden. Good.\n\n- `newSession` click currently closes mobile; fine. Add maybe no session actions.\n\n- Functions:\n```js\n  function openSessionMenu(row, anchor, x, y) {\n    sessionMenuTarget = row;\n    sessionMenuAnchor = anchor || null;\n    if (sessionMenuAnchor) sessionMenuAnchor.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');\n    var left, top;\n    if (typeof x === 'number' && typeof y === 'number') {\n      left = x; top = y;\n    } else {\n      var rect = anchor.getBoundingClientRect();\n      left = rect.right - 176;\n      top = rect.bottom + 4;\n    }\n    left = Math.min(Math.max(8, left), window.innerWidth - 184);\n    top = Math.min(Math.max(8, top), window.innerHeight - 132);\n    sessionMenu.style.left = left + 'px';\n    sessionMenu.style.top = top + 'px';\n    sessionMenu.classList.add('is-open');\n    var first = sessionMenu.querySelector('.menu-item');\n    if (first) first.focus();\n  }\n\n  function closeSessionMenu() {\n    sessionMenu.classList.remove('is-open');\n    if (sessionMenuAnchor) {\n      sessionMenuAnchor.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');\n      sessionMenuAnchor = null;\n    }\n    sessionMenuTarget = null; // but we may need target for actions? Actions fire before close? In menu item handlers, read target first.\n  }\n```\n- Careful: In menu action handler, if we call closeSessionMenu first, it sets `sessionMenuTarget=null`; capture the target before closing. Do:\n```js\n  sessionMenu.querySelectorAll('[data-session-action]').forEach(function (btn) {\n    btn.addEventListener('click', function () {\n      var action = btn.getAttribute('data-session-action');\n      var row = sessionMenuTarget;\n      closeSessionMenu();\n      if (!row) return;\n      if (action === 'rename') startRename(row);\n      else if (action === 'archive') archiveSession(row);\n      else if (action === 'delete') openDeleteDialog(row);\n    });\n  });\n```\n- But `closeSessionMenu` sets `sessionMenuTarget=null`; we captured row. Good.\n- `closeSessionMenu` should not clear `sessionMenuTarget` before actions? Captured.\n- On outside click:\n```js\n  document.addEventListener('click', function (event) {\n    if (!sessionMenu.contains(event.target)) closeSessionMenu();\n  });\n```\n- But the more button click stops propagation, so this won't close it immediately. Right-click doesn't trigger click. Menu items are inside; the document handler sees inside and doesn't close; the menu item handler closes. Good.\n- On scroll:\n```js\n  document.addEventListener('scroll', function () { closeSessionMenu(); }, true);\n```\n- This will fire when the page scrolls; the menu is fixed. Fine.\n- On Esc:\n```js\n  document.addEventListener('keydown', function (event) {\n    if (event.key === 'Escape') {\n      closeSessionMenu();\n      closeDeleteDialog();\n    }\n  });\n```\n- Add to the existing Esc handler? A separate one is fine; both run. The existing handler closes account/mobile. Good.\n- `startRename(row)`:\n```js\n  var renaming = false;\n  function startRename(row) {\n    if (!row) return;\n    var btn = row.querySelector('.session');\n    var title = row.querySelector('.session-title');\n    if (!btn || !title) return;\n    var old = title.textContent;\n    var input = document.createElement('input');\n    input.className = 'session-rename';\n    input.type = 'text';\n    input.value = old;\n    input.setAttribute('aria-label', '重命名会话');\n    row.classList.add('is-renaming');\n    row.appendChild(input);\n    input.focus();\n    input.select();\n    var done = false;\n    function finish(save) {\n      if (done) return;\n      done = true;\n      var next = input.value.trim();\n      if (!save || !next) next = old;\n      title.textContent = next;\n      row.classList.remove('is-renaming');\n      input.remove();\n      var more = row.querySelector('.session-more');\n      if (more) row.insertBefore(btn, more);\n      if (save && next !== old) showToast('会话已重命名');\n    }\n    input.addEventListener('keydown', function (event) {\n      if (event.key === 'Enter') { event.preventDefault(); finish(true); }\n      else if (event.key === 'Escape') { event.preventDefault(); finish(false); }\n    });\n    input.addEventListener('blur', function () { finish(true); });\n  }\n```\n- Wait: `row.appendChild(input)` adds the input after the more button? The row children: btn, more. `appendChild(input)` → btn, more, input. The CSS `.is-renaming .session-more{display:none}` and `.is-renaming .session{display:none}`, so only input visible; good. `btn` is hidden but still in DOM. On finish, `row.insertBefore(btn, more)` moves the button before the more; the input removed; good.\n- But `startRename` is called after `closeSessionMenu`, which sets `sessionMenuTarget=null`; captured row. Good.\n- `btn` is the session button; its title span still there.\n- The `blur` can fire when pressing Enter? Enter handler calls finish and removes the input; the blur may fire, but `done` guards. Good.\n- On Escape, finish false removes; blur may fire, guard.\n- The input click should not trigger the row context? no.\n- After rename, the search filter may be affected; if a search query active, the title might no longer match; should re-run the filter. Not essential. Could call a `filterSessions` function. The search handler is inline. Skipping.\n- The row's session button click listener remains; after reinsert, works. Good.\n- The more button click listener remains. Good.\n- The session button's padding-right 30; good.\n- If the user clicks elsewhere while renaming, blur saves. Good.\n\n- `archiveSession(row)`:\n```js\n  function archiveSession(row) {\n    row.classList.add('is-archived');\n    showToast('会话已归档（原型）');\n  }\n```\n- Maybe change the session meta? Not. The opacity indicates.\n- `openDeleteDialog(row)`:\n```js\n  function openDeleteDialog(row) {\n    deleteSessionTarget = row;\n    var title = row.querySelector('.session-title');\n    deleteSessionName.textContent = title ? title.textContent : '';\n    deleteDialog.classList.add('is-open');\n    var dialog = deleteDialog.querySelector('.dialog');\n    if (dialog) dialog.focus();\n  }\n  function closeDeleteDialog() {\n    deleteDialog.classList.remove('is-open');\n    deleteSessionTarget = null;\n  }\n```\n- Confirm:\n```js\n  confirmDelete.addEventListener('click', function () {\n    var row = deleteSessionTarget;\n    if (!row) { closeDeleteDialog(); return; }\n    var session = row.querySelector('.session');\n    var wasActive = session && session.classList.contains('is-active');\n    row.remove();\n    closeDeleteDialog();\n    var remaining = Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.session'));\n    if (wasActive && remaining.length) {\n      remaining[0].classList.add('is-active');\n      remaining[0].setAttribute('aria-current', 'page');\n    }\n    sessionCount.textContent = String(remaining.length);\n    document.querySelectorAll('.session-group').forEach(function (group) {\n      var has = group.querySelector('.session');\n      group.hidden = !has;\n    });\n    showToast('会话已删除');\n  });\n```\n- If the active session is deleted and the first remaining is in a group; good.\n- If no remaining, the count 0; the chat content remains. Fine.\n- `remaining` includes all sessions (7-1=6). The count. Good.\n- The group labels: group.hidden if no session. Good.\n- If a search filter is active, the remaining count is all sessions, not visible; fine.\n- The target row may have been removed? no.\n- `cancelDelete` closes.\n- Backdrop click:\n```js\n  deleteDialog.addEventListener('click', function (event) {\n    if (event.target === deleteDialog) closeDeleteDialog();\n  });\n```\n- The dialog content click doesn't close.\n- `confirmDelete`/`cancelDelete` vars.\n\n- The session menu actions:\n```js\n  sessionMenu.querySelectorAll('[data-session-action]').forEach(function (btn) {\n    btn.addEventListener('click', function () {\n      var action = btn.getAttribute('data-session-action');\n      var row = sessionMenuTarget;\n      closeSessionMenu();\n      if (!row) return;\n      if (action === 'rename') startRename(row);\n      if (action === 'archive') archiveSession(row);\n      if (action === 'delete') openDeleteDialog(row);\n    });\n  });\n```\n- But `closeSessionMenu` sets `sessionMenuTarget=null`; capture row first. Yes.\n- The menu item click also bubbles to document; document sees inside menu? The menu is still open at the moment of click; closeSessionMenu removes class, then the document click handler runs? Event propagation: the menu item listener runs, closes menu; then document listener runs, `sessionMenu.contains(event.target)` true (the target is still in the DOM, menu hidden), so no extra. Fine.\n- The menu item focus? fine.\n\n- The more button `aria-expanded` toggled. On close, if anchor exists set false; then null. Good.\n- When opening via context menu, anchor null; no aria. Good.\n- If the menu is open and the user right-clicks another row, openSessionMenu replaces target; anchor from previous? If sessionMenuAnchor exists, set its aria false before assigning new? Add at the start of openSessionMenu: if previous anchor, set false. Good.\n```js\n  if (sessionMenuAnchor) sessionMenuAnchor.setAttribute('aria-expanded','false');\n```\n- When opening via more button, set anchor true. When via context, anchor null.\n- The menu pos.\n- `sessionMenu.querySelector('.menu-item').focus()`: focusing a menu item may scroll? The menu fixed; fine.\n- If the user presses Esc while the menu is open, close; if the dialog open, close. The separate Esc handler.\n- The session menu's `role=menu`; the buttons `role=menuitem`. Good.\n- The dialog `aria-modal`; no focus trap. Prototype.\n\n- The menu `z-index:120`; the account menu `z-index:95`; the dialog 130; toast? The toast is fixed bottom, z 100; dialog above; menu above toast. Fine.\n- The sidebar is z20; the menu is fixed at body level (outside app), z120. Good.\n- The dialog outside app, z130. Good.\n\n**Important**: The session menu HTML outside the app but inside body; the CSS `.menu-item` is global and used by account menu and session menu. The `.menu-item` styles have `height:33`, etc. Good.\n- The session menu's menu-sep. Good.\n- The session menu's delete item `.is-danger` uses the account menu `.menu-item.is-danger` style (red). Good.\n\n**Icons**: Add `i-edit`, `i-trash`.\n- The `i-archive` exists; use for 归档.\n- The menu items:\n  - Rename: i-edit.\n  - Archive: i-archive.\n  - Delete: i-trash.\n\n**HTML placement**: Before toast:\n```html\n<div class=\"session-menu\" id=\"sessionMenu\" ...>...</div>\n<div class=\"dialog-backdrop\" id=\"deleteDialog\">...</div>\n```\n- The toast is `<div class=\"toast\" id=\"toast\">`. Add before it.\n- The menu's items with `data-session-action`.\n\n**JS placement**: Add variables and functions after the sidebar/account code, before session list? The wrapping code runs in the session list block; the functions can be declared later (hoisted). The menu/dialog variables must be defined before the functions run; they can be at the top with other vars. Add to the var block:\n```js\n  var sessionMenu = ...\n  var sessionCount = ...\n  var deleteDialog = ...\n  var deleteSessionName = ...\n  var confirmDelete = ...\n  var cancelDelete = ...\n  var sessionMenuTarget = null;\n  var sessionMenuAnchor = null;\n  var deleteSessionTarget = null;\n```\n- The functions can be defined after the sidebar block, before the session list; or after. Function declarations hoisted. The event listeners for menu/dialog can be added after the session block. Fine.\n- The wrapping code calls openSessionMenu (hoisted).\n- The menu item listeners need to be attached; add after the wrap or later. If added later, fine.\n- The confirm/cancel listeners later.\n- The document listeners later.\n- The Escape listener later.\n\nLet's patch HTML/JS.\n\nFirst add icons and HTML menu/dialog. Then JS.\n\nUse exact anchors.\n\nFor the icon insertion, add after `i-archive` or `i-logout`:\n- `i-edit`, `i-trash`.\n\nHTML insertion before toast:\n```html\n<div class=\"session-menu\" id=\"sessionMenu\" role=\"menu\" aria-label=\"会话操作\">\n  <button class=\"menu-item\" role=\"menuitem\" data-session-action=\"rename\">\n    <svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-edit\"/></svg>重命名\n  </button>\n  <button class=\"menu-item\" role=\"menuitem\" data-session-action=\"archive\">\n    <svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-archive\"/></svg>归档\n  </button>\n  <div class=\"menu-sep\"></div>\n  <button class=\"menu-item is-danger\" role=\"menuitem\" data-session-action=\"delete\">\n    <svg class=\"ic\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-trash\"/></svg>删除会话\n  </button>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"dialog-backdrop\" id=\"deleteDialog\">\n  <div class=\"dialog\" role=\"dialog\" aria-modal=\"true\" aria-labelledby=\"deleteTitle\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n    <h2 id=\"deleteTitle\">删除会话？</h2>\n    <p>“<span id=\"deleteSessionName\"></span>”及其消息将被删除，此操作不可撤销。</p>\n    <div class=\"dialog-actions\">\n      <button class=\"btn btn-outline\" id=\"cancelDelete\">取消</button>\n      <button class=\"btn btn-danger\" id=\"confirmDelete\">删除会话</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n- The `.dialog` needs focus; tabindex -1.\n- The text has Chinese quotes; fine.\n- The `deleteSessionName` span.\n\nAdd CSS for `.session-menu .menu-item` maybe the account menu `.menu-item` base has `height:33`; we set 32. Good.\n- The menu items' text color; fine.\n- The `.menu-sep` margin. Good.\n- The menu's `.menu-item` has `width:100%`; good.\n- The `.session-menu` is display none; `.is-open` block.\n- The `.dialog` has no max-height; fine.\n\nAdd JS.\n\nLet's do the HTML/CSS first."}}},{"type":"chunk","time":1793893782621,"chunk":{"type":"block-start","index":1,"blockType":"tool-call"}},{"type":"tool-call-chunks","time0":1793893782621,"index":1,"dt":[],"id":"call_00_fNjrpz6UVIssLtOJm9La5000","name":"bash","args":[""]},{"type":"tool-call-chunks","time0":1793