{"type":"assistant/message","seq":721,"time":1793893907533,"data":{"turn":5,"step":4,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"Now think about bugs in v5 session actions:\n\n1. The `sessionMenu` HTML is outside `.app`, before the toast. The CSS `.session-menu` position fixed; good.\n2. The `deleteDialog` outside app. Good.\n3. The session menu uses `.menu-item` styles; `.menu-item` global. Good.\n4. The icons `i-edit`, `i-trash` added. Good.\n5. The more button wrapping happens after the array. Good.\n6. **Potential issue**: The `.session` button click handler is attached after wrapping. When clicking the more button, the event is on the sibling; no session click. Good.\n7. **Potential issue**: Right-clicking the session row triggers contextmenu; the browser context menu suppressed. Good.\n8. **Potential issue**: The more button is visible on hover; on the active session, the more button might overlap the title? The session has padding-right 30; good.\n9. **Potential issue**: The CSS `.session-row .session{padding-right:30px}` overrides the base `.session` padding? The shorthand `padding:8px 8px 8px 10px` in `.session` sets all; `.session-row .session` specificity (0,2,0) vs `.session` (0,1,0), so the padding-right 30 applies while other sides remain from `.session`. Good.\n10. **Potential issue**: The `.session-more` top 7, right 4; the session row; good.\n11. **Potential issue**: The session menu is fixed; the more button click stops propagation; document click doesn't close. Good.\n12. **Potential issue**: The more button click opens the menu; then `document.addEventListener('click')` still runs? `stopPropagation` prevents. Good.\n13. **Potential issue**: Right-click opens the menu; then a click event on document might close it? Right-click doesn't fire click; fine.\n14. **Potential issue**: Clicking a menu item: the menu item handler captures row, calls closeSessionMenu (removes class, sets target null, aria false), then startRename/archive/delete. Good.\n15. **Potential issue**: The document click listener runs after the menu item click; `sessionMenu.contains(event.target)` is still true (menu hidden but element exists), so it doesn't close again. Good.\n16. **Potential issue**: The menu item click on delete opens the dialog; the dialog is displayed; the session menu hidden. Good.\n17. **Potential issue**: The delete dialog backdrop click closes; the dialog buttons are inside; event target is the button, not backdrop; fine.\n18. **Potential issue**: Confirm delete: row.remove; closeDialog; remaining; if wasActive, activate remaining[0]. The remaining[0] may be a hidden session (if a search filter active). It still becomes active; fine. The count all remaining. The groups hidden if no sessions. Good.\n19. **Potential issue**: If the active session is deleted, the chat content still refers to it. Prototype. Could show a toast. Fine.\n20. **Potential issue**: If the deleted row is the only one in a group, the group hidden. The `.group-label` inside the group; hidden. Good.\n21. **Potential issue**: The session count id is in the sidebar. Good.\n22. **Potential issue**: The search filter after wrapping: It hides the row; the group visibility check uses `group.querySelectorAll('.session')` and `s.hidden`. Since we set `item.hidden`, good.\n23. **Potential issue**: The search filter's `sessions` array includes removed sessions; after delete, the input event loops detached items; `item.hidden` set; `item.closest('.session-row')` returns null; fine. The group visibility uses DOM. Good.\n24. **Potential issue**: The `sessionMenuTarget` is set null by closeSessionMenu before startRename; we captured row. Good.\n25. **Potential issue**: `startRename` row: It hides the session button via CSS `.is-renaming .session{display:none}` and the more; appends input. The input width 100%. The row is inside the session group; the input appears. Good.\n   - On finish, `row.insertBefore(btn, more)`; the btn was already before more; it moves. The input removed. The `is-renaming` class removed. Good.\n   - The input blur calls finish(true); if the user clicks the more button, the more is hidden, so not. If clicks elsewhere, save. Good.\n   - The input's `keydown` Enter triggers finish; the input removed; blur perhaps fires; done guard.\n   - The input's Escape triggers finish(false); the input removed; blur guard.\n   - The title text updates. Good.\n   - The session button's click listener remains. Good.\n   - The more button's listener remains. Good.\n   - The row's contextmenu remains. Good.\n26. **Potential issue**: The rename input is appended after the more button; the more is hidden. The input width 100%; the row may have the session hidden. Good.\n27. **Potential issue**: The rename input's margin 3px 0; the row height. Fine.\n28. **Potential issue**: The session menu first item focus; if the menu is opened via right-click, focusing the first item is okay. The menu item's focus may trigger the session row's focus-within, showing the more; fine.\n29. **Potential issue**: On scroll, the menu closes; the `document.addEventListener('scroll', ..., true)` with capture catches scrolls in the session list and page. Good.\n30. **Potential issue**: On opening the menu, `sessionMenu.style.left/top`; if the menu is inside body but the body has `overflow:hidden`, fixed still. Good.\n31. **Potential issue**: The menu width 176; clamp `window.innerWidth - 184`; good.\n32. **Potential issue**: The menu height ~5 padding + 32+32+sep+32 = ~110; clamp top `innerHeight - 132`; good.\n33. **Potential issue**: The menu z-index 120; the dialog 130; the toast 100; good.\n34. **Potential issue**: The menu's `.menu-item` base has `height:33`; we override 32. Good.\n35. **Potential issue**: The menu's `.menu-item` icon width 14; good.\n36. **Potential issue**: The menu's `menu-sep` margin; good.\n37. **Potential issue**: The dialog's `.btn-danger` added; `.btn` base from v4 uses `.btn-primary`, `.btn-outline`; `.btn-danger` inherits `.btn` only if class includes `btn btn-danger`; the HTML has `class=\"btn btn-danger\"`. Good.\n38. **Potential issue**: The dialog's `.dialog h2` etc. good.\n39. **Potential issue**: The dialog's `tabindex=\"-1\"` and focus; good.\n40. **Potential issue**: The dialog backdrop `display:none`; `.is-open` grid. Good.\n41. **Potential issue**: The dialog backdrop has `backdrop-filter`; fine.\n42. **Potential issue**: The dialog's click outside closes; the dialog itself is a child; clicking inside (on padding) bubbles to backdrop? The event target would be `.dialog` or its child, not `deleteDialog`, so no close. Good.\n43. **Potential issue**: The dialog cancel/confirm buttons; good.\n44. **Potential issue**: The session menu and dialog are outside `.app`; the app has height 100dvh; body overflow hidden. The menu fixed; dialog fixed. Good.\n45. **Potential issue**: The session menu `role=menu` with `.menu-item` buttons; good.\n46. **Potential issue**: The session more button `aria-haspopup=menu`, `aria-expanded` updated. Good.\n47. **Potential issue**: If the menu is opened via context menu, no anchor; `aria-expanded` on the more button not set. The more button's aria-expanded remains false even though the menu is open. This is a minor a11y inconsistency. The menu is not anchored to a specific button (right-click). Fine. The more button click path sets aria. Good.\n48. **Potential issue**: `closeSessionMenu` sets the anchor aria false. Good.\n49. **Potential issue**: The session menu target and anchor are reset. Good.\n50. **Potential issue**: The `sessionMenu` focus on first item; if the user presses Tab, focus moves; fine.\n51. **Potential issue**: The `document.addEventListener('keydown')` for Escape closes the menu/dialog; the existing handler for account/mobile also runs. Good.\n52. **Potential issue**: The session menu opens while the account menu is open? Both could be open; clicking the more button in the sidebar would trigger the document click handler closing the account menu (target not in account menu/btn), then open the session menu. Good.\n53. **Potential issue**: The account menu opens while the session menu is open; clicking the account button triggers document click closing session menu (target not in session menu), then opens account menu. Good.\n54. **Potential issue**: The session menu's `document.click` listener is added before the existing account menu document click listener? The order: account menu listener added in sidebar block; session menu listener added later. Both run. Fine.\n55. **Potential issue**: The session menu item click on \"删除\" opens the dialog; the document click listener for account menu might close the account menu (already closed) and the session menu; fine.\n56. **Potential issue**: The dialog open while the session menu is closed. Good.\n57. **Potential issue**: The delete dialog's `closeDeleteDialog` called by cancel; focus? Fine.\n58. **Potential issue**: The `sessionCount` count after delete uses all `.session` elements; if the search filter hidden some, the count is still total. Good.\n59. **Potential issue**: The groups hidden if no sessions; if a group hidden due to search, then after clearing search the group is shown? The search handler sets `group.hidden = !visible`; good. After delete, groups with no sessions hidden; clearing search doesn't unhide empty groups? The search handler `groups.forEach` sets `group.hidden = !visible`; for an empty group, visible false, hidden true. Fine. Groups with sessions show. Good.\n60. **Potential issue**: The session count header is `7`; after delete 6. Good.\n\n**One bug**: The `openSessionMenu` function is declared after the session wrapping loop (we inserted it before newSession, which is after the sessions click loop, but function declarations are hoisted). Fine.\n\n**One bug**: In `startRename`, `row.appendChild(input)` after the more button. The CSS `.is-renaming .session-more{display:none}` and `.is-renaming .session{display:none}`. The input is visible. On finish, `row.insertBefore(btn, more)` moves btn before more; but the input was appended after more; we remove it. Good.\n- The row's `is-renaming` class removed. Good.\n\n**One bug**: The `blur` handler `finish(true)` fires if the user clicks the session menu? The more button is hidden. If the user clicks another session, the rename saves. Good.\n\n**One bug**: The `startRename` uses the title element and updates it. The title's `textContent`; good.\n\n**One bug**: The `archiveSession` only adds class; the row's opacity .55. It doesn't change the meta. Fine.\n\n**One bug**: The `openDeleteDialog` focus the `.dialog`; the dialog has tabindex -1. Good.\n- The active element after close may be body; fine.\n\n**One bug**: The `confirmDelete` activates `remaining[0]` but the session click handler's active state removal loop was only triggered by clicks, not here. We add is-active to remaining[0]; the deleted row removed. Any other active? Only the deleted row was active. Fine.\n- The `aria-current` on the deleted row removed with it. Good.\n- The other sessions have no aria-current. Good.\n- If the deleted row was not active, no active change. Good.\n- If the active row deleted and remaining[0] is in a different group, active. Fine.\n\n**One bug**: The session menu's position when opened via the more button: `left = rect.right - 176`. The more button is at the right edge of the sidebar; rect.right ~ sidebar width - 4; left ~ 288-4-176=108. The menu fits. On mobile, right ~ sidebar 288; left ~ 108; fits. Good.\n- The menu top = more rect.bottom + 4; the row near the bottom may clamp to viewport - 132. Good.\n\n**One bug**: The session menu left/top are fixed; if the page is scrolled (the session list scroll), the row rect is viewport-based; good. The scroll listener closes the menu on any scroll; fine.\n\n**One bug**: The session menu HTML is before the toast but outside `.app`; the fixed position; good.\n\n**One bug**: The `.session-menu .menu-item` uses the account menu `.menu-item` styles; the account menu is hidden but the class styles apply. Good.\n\n**One bug**: The `.session-menu` is a div with `role=menu`; the `.menu-item` buttons have `role=menuitem`. Good.\n\n**One bug**: The session menu's `menu-sep` uses `.menu-sep` styles (height 1, margin 5 4, background line-2). Good.\n\n**One bug**: The `.dialog` uses `.btn-outline`/`.btn-danger`; `.btn` base. Good.\n\n**One bug**: The `.dialog-backdrop` `display:none`; `.is-open` grid. The `hidden` attribute not used. Good.\n\n**One bug**: The `deleteDialog.addEventListener('click')` checks `event.target === deleteDialog`; the backdrop is the div; clicking the padding outside the dialog (the backdrop) closes. Good.\n\n**One bug**: The dialog's `.dialog` has `outline:none`; focus visible? The focus ring is suppressed for the dialog; fine.\n\n**One bug**: The session menu's focus: `first.focus()`; the menu item has no tabindex, but buttons are focusable. Good.\n\n**One bug**: The `session-more` button is visible on hover; on keyboard focus within the row, visible. The session button itself is focusable; tab to the more. Good.\n\n**One bug**: The right-click on the row while the more button is not visible still opens. Good.\n\n**One bug**: The `session-more` is inside the row after the session button; the row has no explicit height; the session button defines. The more absolute. Good.\n\n**One bug**: The `.session-row.is-archived .session{opacity:.55}`; the more still visible. Fine.\n\n**One bug**: The `.session-row.is-renaming .session{display:none}` and the input appended; the row's height maybe 40; fine.\n\n**One bug**: The search input `q` filter: after wrapping, `item.hidden = !match` hides the button; the row hidden; the group visibility uses `s.hidden`. Good.\n- The group labels: if a group hidden by search and then the query cleared, the handler sets group.hidden = !visible; visible true; show. Good.\n- If a group was hidden by delete (empty), the search handler won't unhide (visible false), fine.\n\n**One bug**: The `sessionCount` after delete counts all sessions, including those hidden by search; fine.\n\n**One bug**: The nav links to pages file; the pages file pending. We'll create it.\n\n**One bug**: The account menu \"设置\" anchor to pages; clicking triggers the menu item close listener (setAccountMenu false) and navigates. Good.\n- The account menu \"账号\" still data-demo. Fine.\n\n**One bug**: The nav anchors \"智能体/任务/知识库\" use `.sb-nav-item`; the JS `document.querySelectorAll('.sb-nav-item')` attaches click listeners to close the mobile drawer. For anchors, the click listener runs, closes the drawer, and then navigation. Good.\n- The `.sb-nav-item` active? The chat page's \"对话\" is active; the anchors are not. Good.\n- On mobile, clicking a nav link closes the drawer then navigates. Fine.\n\n**One bug**: The `data-demo` handler no longer attaches to the nav anchors (no data-demo); fine.\n\n**One bug**: The account menu item \"设置\" is an anchor with class `menu-item`; the menu item close listener attaches; clicking navigates. Good.\n- The data-demo handler doesn't include it; no toast. Good.\n\n**One bug**: The pages file's account menu settings will switch pages; later.\n\nNow the pages file. This is the big new deliverable.\n\nLet's design and write. We can reuse v5 CSS for the sidebar, tokens, base. Instead of copying 1000 lines manually, we can copy the shared CSS from v5 and append page CSS. But v5's CSS includes chat-specific styles (timeline, composer, trace, approval, etc.) and page-specific. Copying all would work but bloat; the pages file could still include unused CSS, not a problem for a prototype. It might be simpler to copy v5's entire `<style>` and HTML shell, then replace the main chat with the pages. But v5's JS chat logic would need replacement. We could copy v5 and remove the chat content, leaving the sidebar and adding pages. That is actually easier:\n1. Copy v5 to `ui-v5-pages.html`.\n2. Replace the `<main class=\"chat\">...</main>` and trace with a new `<main class=\"page-main\">` containing pages.\n3. Remove chat-specific JS (trace, approval, composer, send, conversation) and keep sidebar/account/session logic (maybe adapt).\n4. Add page-specific CSS and JS.\n5. The v5 CSS includes chat/timeline/composer/trace styles unused; harmless but large. The sidebar CSS is already there. This saves rewriting the sidebar CSS. The file will be ~120KB; fine for a prototype.\n6. The v5 CSS includes `.app` 3-column grid with trace. For the pages file, set `.app{grid-template-columns:var(--sidebar-w) minmax(0,1fr)}` and remove trace. We can override `.app` and hide `.trace` (not present). The `--trace-w` unused.\n7. The page main uses `page-*` CSS; add it.\n8. The v5 CSS has `.chat` etc.; unused.\n9. The v5 JS has chat logic; we need to remove/disable it. Could keep some portions? The sidebar/account/session logic is intertwined with chat logic. Let's inspect:\n   - Elements: stream, conversation, input, sendBtn, approvalCard, approvalStatus, resolvedText, traceToggle, runStatus, runDot, runStatusText, usageLabel, etc. In the pages file, these elements won't exist; the JS `document.getElementById` returns null and `.addEventListener` will throw, breaking all JS. So we must remove or guard.\n   - We could replace the entire `<script>` with a new pages JS, reusing the sidebar/account/menu/session code. That's cleaner.\n10. The sidebar HTML can be copied from v5, but the nav items should be buttons with data-page (not anchors), and the \"对话\" anchor to ui-v5.html. The account menu settings data-page. The session items can be static or link to chat. The session menu/delete could be included too, but maybe keep the session list static. The user's session action is in v5; the pages file can have the same sidebar visual. To reduce JS, the pages sidebar session list can be buttons that navigate to chat. The more/delete not implemented. But the sidebar HTML from v5 includes the session menu/dialog at body end; we can remove them.\n11. The pages file's sidebar should have the same styles and the account menu. The v5 CSS supports.\n12. The `.app` in v5 has 3 columns; override to 2. The v5 `.app.sidebar-collapsed` etc. include trace; need override.\n13. The v5 responsive CSS includes trace rules; with no trace, harmless. The `.app` at ≤1180 sets sidebar + chat; at ≤900 sidebar drawer; good. The `.chat` rules unused. The `.page-main` new.\n14. The v5 CSS has `.sidebar` z20; good.\n15. The page main needs to fit in the second grid column; `.page-main` flex. The `.app` height 100dvh; good.\n16. The v5 CSS's `.chat` styles not applied.\n17. The v5 CSS's `.trace` not present.\n18. The v5 CSS's `@media` for `.app` at ≤1180 uses two columns (sidebar + chat) — that's exactly the pages layout. At >1180, v5 `.app` has 3 columns; we need override to 2. At ≤1180, v5 `.app` is 2 columns; good. At ≤900, one column and sidebar drawer; good. At ≤760, v5 has `.chat` rules only; page main unaffected; need mobile page styles.\n19. The v5 CSS's `.app.trace-collapsed` etc. unused; no trace. Fine.\n20. The v5 CSS's `.page-main` new.\n\nThis copy-and-replace approach saves a lot of CSS. The file will include unused chat CSS but that's acceptable for a prototype. The user cares about the visual.\n\n**Steps for pages file**:\n1. Copy `ui-v5.html` → `ui-v5-pages.html`.\n2. Change title/comment.\n3. Replace `<main class=\"chat\"> ... </main>` and `<aside class=\"trace\"> ... </aside>` with new page main. The trace is after main; remove it.\n4. Keep the sidebar; adjust nav:\n   - \"对话\" becomes `<a class=\"sb-nav-item\" href=\"ui-v5.html\">`.\n   - \"智能体\" button with data-page=\"agents\" and active by default.\n   - \"任务\" data-page=\"tasks\".\n   - \"知识库\" data-page=\"knowledge\".\n   - The \"对话\" active class removed; the \"智能体\" active initially. The page router sets active.\n   - The newSession button: could link to ui-v5.html; keep button with JS navigate? The pages JS can handle. Or change to anchor. Use a button; JS `window.location.href='ui-v5.html'`.\n   - The session list items: clicking should navigate to ui-v5.html. The pages JS can attach. Or leave static. We'll attach.\n   - The account menu: \"设置\" button data-page=\"settings\"; \"账号\" button data-page=\"settings\" maybe.\n   - The account menu \"设置\" currently anchor to ui-v5-pages.html#settings (self); we can change to data-page.\n5. Remove the session menu/dialog from the pages file (or keep and implement; not necessary). The v5 CSS for them is unused. The HTML menu/dialog can be removed.\n6. Replace the `<script>` entirely with pages JS. Use the sidebar/account/session code from v5 but remove chat/approval/session menu/dialog code. The session list can navigate to chat.\n7. Add page CSS before the reduced-motion or at the end of the style. Since the v5 CSS is large, append a new `<style>` block after the existing one? Simpler: add a second `<style>` block in the head after the first. CSS cascade works. This avoids editing the huge existing style. Add `<style id=\"pages-css\">...page styles + overrides...</style>` after the first style. The overrides:\n   - `.app{grid-template-columns:var(--sidebar-w) minmax(0,1fr)}` at all widths; but the v5 responsive media queries will later set `.app` at ≤1180 2 cols, ≤900 1 col. The order of the second style block after the first means its base `.app` 2-col overrides the first base 3-col; but the first's media queries (inside the first style) come before the second style block, so the second base `.app` overrides even at ≤900? CSS cascade: all rules in the first style, then all in the second. The first's media query `.app{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}` at ≤900 is in the first style, but the second style's base `.app{2 cols}` comes later and would override at all widths, breaking mobile. Need to handle:\n     - Put the override `.app{...}` in the second style with its own media queries replicating the responsive behavior.\n     - Or edit the v5 CSS's base `.app` and media queries in the pages file. Since it's a copy, we can patch:\n       - Base `.app{grid-template-columns:var(--sidebar-w) minmax(0,1fr) var(--trace-w)}` → `var(--sidebar-w) minmax(0,1fr)`.\n       - `.app.trace-collapsed`, `.app.sidebar-collapsed` (with trace) adjust.\n       - The 1180 media `.app` already 2 cols; fine.\n       - The 900 media 1 col; fine.\n       - The `.app.sidebar-collapsed` at >1180 would be `56px 1fr 332`; need `56px 1fr`. Patch.\n       - The `.app.trace-collapsed` unused; can leave.\n       - The `.trace` rules unused.\n     - Easier: patch the base `.app` and `.app.sidebar-collapsed` in the copied CSS; the media queries at 1180/900 already correct.\n   - Add page CSS in a second `<style>` block; its base `.page` etc. won't conflict with `.app` if we don't redefine `.app` there. Good.\n8. The v5 HTML `<div class=\"app\" id=\"app\">` contains sidebar + scrim + main + trace. Replace main/trace with page main. The scrim remains. Good.\n9. The v5 JS's sidebar/account logic can be adapted. Replace the script.\n\nThis approach is efficient.\n\n**Page main HTML**:\n```html\n<main class=\"page-main\">\n  <div class=\"page-topbar\">\n    <button class=\"mobile-sidebar-btn\" id=\"mobileSidebarBtn\" ...>\n      <svg menu>\n    </button>\n    <span class=\"page-topbar-title\" id=\"mobilePageTitle\">智能体</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"page-scroll\" id=\"pageScroll\">\n\n    <section class=\"page\" id=\"page-agents\" data-page=\"agents\"> ... </section>\n    <section class=\"page\" id=\"page-tasks\" data-page=\"tasks\" hidden> ... </section>\n    <section class=\"page\" id=\"page-knowledge\" data-page=\"knowledge\" hidden> ... </section>\n    <section class=\"page\" id=\"page-settings\" data-page=\"settings\" hidden> ... </section>\n\n  </div>\n</main>\n```\n- The `hidden` attribute plus `.page[hidden]{display:none}`; the page router toggles `hidden`.\n- The `.page-topbar` is sticky; on desktop hidden.\n- The `page-scroll` scrolls. On mobile, the topbar outside the scroll or inside? If the topbar is a flex child before the scroll, it stays fixed at top; good.\n- On desktop, topbar display none; scroll fills.\n- The `.page-main` height 100dvh; flex column.\n- The `.page` max width; padding.\n\n**Page header**:\n```html\n<header class=\"page-head\">\n  <div class=\"page-heading\">\n    <h1 class=\"page-title\">智能体</h1>\n    <p class=\"page-sub\">管理通过 A2A 注册的远程智能体，查看 Agent Card 与健康状态。</p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"page-actions\">\n    <button class=\"btn btn-outline\" data-demo=\"刷新全部（原型演示）\">刷新</button>\n    <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" id=\"registerAgentBtn\">+ 注册智能体</button>\n  </div>\n</header>\n```\n- Use `.btn` from v5 CSS; `.btn-primary`/outline exist. Good.\n- The `.page-actions` CSS new.\n- The primary button plus sign in text; okay.\n\n**Stats**:\n```html\n<div class=\"stats\">\n  <div class=\"stat\"><span class=\"stat-value\">3</span><span class=\"stat-label\">已注册</span></div>\n  <div class=\"stat\"><span class=\"stat-value\">2</span><span class=\"stat-label\">健康</span></div>\n  <div class=\"stat\"><span class=\"stat-value\">1</span><span class=\"stat-label\">降级</span></div>\n  <div class=\"stat\"><span class=\"stat-value\">3</span><span class=\"stat-label\">已启用</span></div>\n</div>\n```\n- Use `.stat-value` mono 22; `.stat-label` 10.5. Good.\n- The stats could be a row with dividers. Good.\n\n**Toolbar**:\n```html\n<div class=\"toolbar\">\n  <div class=\"seg\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"筛选智能体\">\n    <button class=\"is-active\">全部 <span>3</span></button>\n    <button>健康 <span>2</span></button>\n    <button>降级 <span>1</span></button>\n    <button>已禁用 <span>0</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <label class=\"tool-search\">\n    <svg search>\n    <input placeholder=\"搜索名称或 slug\">\n  </label>\n</div>\n```\n- The segmented buttons; no JS filter for agents? Could implement a simple filter? The user wants samples; not necessary. But the tabs should look interactive. Add JS for agents filter by health? Could implement:\n  - Each agent item has `data-health=\"healthy|degraded|disabled\"`; filter buttons data-filter. Hide items.\n  - Search filter by name/slug.\n  - This is easy.\n  - The counts.\n- Use `data-filter` on seg buttons.\n- The search input id `agentSearch`.\n- JS.\n\n**Register panel**:\n- A hidden panel toggled by the button. Good.\n- It is a form with inputs. Use `.register-panel` CSS.\n- The button toggles; JS.\n- The \"拉取 Agent Card\" and \"注册\" buttons data-demo; the register button can hide the panel and toast. Add JS for the toggle only.\n\n**Agent list**:\n- Use `<div class=\"agent-list\">` with `<details class=\"agent-item\" data-health=\"healthy\" open>`.\n- Summary:\n```html\n<summary>\n  <span class=\"agent-badge\">DA</span>\n  <span class=\"agent-main\">\n    <span class=\"agent-name\">data-analyst</span>\n    <span class=\"agent-slug\">data-analyst · A2A 1.0</span>\n  </span>\n  <span class=\"agent-endpoint\">https://data.example.com/a2a</span>\n  <span class=\"agent-skill-count\">2 skills</span>\n  <span class=\"agent-health\"><span class=\"st st-ok\"><span class=\"dot is-ok\"></span>健康</span></span>\n  <svg chevron>\n</summary>\n```\n- The grid columns; the badge; the main; endpoint; skills; health; chevron.\n- The `<details>` summary default marker hidden.\n- The detailed content:\n```html\n<div class=\"agent-detail\">\n  <div class=\"detail-block\">\n    <h4>技能</h4>\n    <div class=\"skill-list\">\n      <span class=\"skill-chip\">verify_numbers</span>\n      <span class=\"skill-chip\">analyze_tickets</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"detail-block\">\n    <h4>连接</h4>\n    <dl class=\"kv\">\n      <dt>协议</dt><dd>A2A 1.0 · JSON-RPC</dd>\n      <dt>鉴权</dt><dd><span class=\"mono\">bearer</span> · <span class=\"mono\">env:DATA_AGENT_KEY</span></dd>\n      <dt>最近检查</dt><dd>23:41:08 · 200 OK · 142ms</dd>\n    </dl>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"detail-block wide\">\n    <h4>操作</h4>\n    <div class=\"detail-actions\">\n      <button class=\"btn btn-outline btn-sm\" data-demo=\"健康检查（原型演示）\">健康检查</button>\n      <button class=\"btn btn-outline btn-sm\" data-demo=\"刷新 Agent Card（原型演示）\">刷新 Card</button>\n      <button class=\"btn btn-ghost btn-sm\" data-demo=\"禁用智能体（原型演示）\">禁用</button>\n      <button class=\"btn btn-ghost btn-sm is-danger-text\" data-demo=\"删除智能体（原型演示）\">删除</button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n- The `.agent-detail` grid 2 columns; the actions block span 2.\n- The `.btn-sm` styles new.\n- The `.btn-ghost` from v5? It exists in the chat composer? v5 CSS has `.btn-ghost`? It has `.btn` base, `.composer-tool`; the `.btn-ghost` from v2? Let's check. v4 CSS has `.btn`, `.btn-primary`, `.btn-outline`; `.btn-ghost` was in the A2A card CSS (v2) maybe still. It might exist. To be safe, define `.btn-ghost` in page CSS.\n- The `.is-danger-text` red.\n- The actions use data-demo; the pages JS attaches the data-demo handler.\n- The row summary is clickable to expand; the action buttons are outside summary (in detail), so fine.\n- The agent list rows.\n- For `code-assistant` degraded, the detail actions similar; health chip amber \"降级\"; data-health=\"degraded\".\n- The `editorial-reviewer` healthy.\n- The list maybe 3 rows.\n- The first row open.\n- The summary grid: 7 columns may be too many; at 1080 content, 36+main 340+endpoint 260+skills 60+health 80+chev 14+gaps 6*14=84 = 874; fits. At 900, hide endpoint maybe. Responsive.\n- Use `.agent-endpoint` ellipsis.\n- The health chip.\n\n**Page CSS** for agents:\n- `.agent-list`, `.agent-item`, `.agent-item summary`, `.agent-badge`, `.agent-main`, `.agent-name`, `.agent-slug`, `.agent-endpoint`, `.agent-skill-count`, `.agent-health`, `.agent-chev`, `.agent-detail`, `.detail-block`, `.detail-block h4`, `.skill-list`, `.skill-chip`, `.kv` (already exists in v5 CSS), `.detail-actions`, `.btn-sm`.\n- The `.kv` from v5 has dt/dd; good.\n- The `.agent-item[open] .agent-chev{transform:rotate(180deg)}`.\n- The summary hover.\n- The summary focus.\n\n**Tasks page content**:\nHeader, stats, toolbar, table.\n- `.task-table` wrapper.\n- `.task-head` grid columns: `minmax(0,1.2fr) minmax(0,1fr) 90px 70px minmax(0,1.2fr)`.\n- Each `<details class=\"task-item\" data-state=\"working\" open>`:\n  - `<summary class=\"task-row\">`\n    - `<span class=\"task-main\"><span class=\"task-id mono\">task_2e91</span><span class=\"task-skill\">review_copy</span></span>`\n    - `<span class=\"task-agent\">editorial-reviewer <small>a2a</small></span>`\n    - `<span class=\"st st-live\">运行中</span>`\n    - `<span class=\"task-duration mono\">00:12</span>`\n    - `<span class=\"task-conv\">退款政策变更的影响面</span>`\n  - `<div class=\"task-detail\">...`\n- The summary grid; the chevron? Add a chevron at the end? The grid has 5 columns; maybe include a chevron in the last? Could add a 6th 14px column. Or the conversation cell with a chevron. Use 6 columns: task, agent, status, duration, conversation, chevron.\n- The header 6 columns accordingly.\n- The detail:\n  - `grid-template-columns: 1.2fr .8fr`:\n    - Request: skill, params, run id, message.\n    - State timeline: submitted/working with times.\n    - Artifact: for completed/failed; for working \"尚未产出\".\n    - Actions: 取消任务 (working) / 打开会话.\n  - For the working task, the cancel button is a `.btn btn-outline is-danger-text`.\n  - The timeline vertical with dots.\n- Task rows:\n  - working: editorial-reviewer, review_copy, 00:12, 退款政策变更的影响面, open.\n  - completed: editorial-reviewer, review_copy, 1.8s, Q3 客服工单周报.\n  - completed: data-analyst, verify_numbers, 1.2s, Q3 客服工单周报.\n  - failed: code-assistant, review_code, 6.4s, 审查：payment 模块重试逻辑.\n- Stats: 4 / 1 / 2 / 1.\n- Filter JS:\n  - `.seg` buttons with data-state = all/working/completed/failed.\n  - `.task-item` data-state.\n  - Hide.\n  - Update active.\n- The table header remains.\n- The task rows are details; clicking expands.\n- The filter counts.\n- The search input? Could include \"搜索任务 ID\" but no JS. Maybe skip search to keep the toolbar focused; add a search that filters by text. Could implement:\n  - `input#taskSearch`; on input, filter by text content. Combine with state filter. More JS. Not necessary. Use only the state filter; the page is a sample.\n- The toolbar right could show \"按 run 分组\" toggle? Skip.\n\n**Knowledge page content**:\nHeader, stats, grid.\n- `.knowledge-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.5fr) minmax(320px,.9fr);gap:28px;align-items:start}`\n- Left `.panel`:\n  - `.panel-head`: h2 \"文档\" + count \"128\"; actions (search input).\n  - `.doc-toolbar`: search input, category select.\n  - `.doc-list`: 5 rows.\n    - `.doc-row`: status dot/chip, title + meta, status chip.\n    - Perhaps a table header? Use a list.\n  - `.panel-foot`: \"显示 5 / 128 · 查看全部\".\n- Right `.panel debug-panel`:\n  - `.panel-head`: h2 \"检索调试\" + a small tag \"pgvector\".\n  - `.debug-desc`: \"直接调用 knowledge/search，验证召回与相似度。\"\n  - `.debug-form`: textarea/input query; row with select top_k, select category, button 检索.\n  - `.debug-results`: 3 `.hit` rows with title + score + source + excerpt.\n  - `.debug-meta`: \"42ms · top_k=5 · cosine\".\n- The left panel could have a top upload strip? The page header upload button. Good.\n- The `.doc-row`:\n  ```html\n  <div class=\"doc-row\">\n    <div class=\"doc-main\">\n      <div class=\"doc-title\">Q3 客服复盘 v2</div>\n      <div class=\"doc-meta\">客服 · 24 chunks · 09-30 更新</div>\n    </div>\n    <span class=\"st st-ok\">就绪</span>\n  </div>\n  ```\n- Statuses: ready (green), indexing (amber), failed (red).\n- The document list left; the retrieval right.\n- The retrieval results use `.result` with title, score, source, excerpt. The `.result-excerpt` small.\n- The panel backgrounds surface; border; radius 8. This is a card, but the design uses panels; okay. Avoid excessive cards. Two panels.\n- The page header stats.\n- The query input prefilled.\n- The search button data-demo; maybe JS updates the elapsed? Not necessary. Could add a toast.\n- The upload button data-demo.\n- The category select.\n- The retrieval panel sticky.\n- Responsive: stack at ≤1100? The content max 1080; at 1180 available 908, the grid 1.5/0.9 with 28 gap → 540/340. Fine. At 900, stack.\n- The page content width 1080; at 1440, sidebar 288, content 1152, page max 1080, left/right margins. The grid left 640, right 400. Good.\n\n**Settings page content**:\n- `.settings-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:150px minmax(0,1fr);gap:32px;align-items:start}`\n- `.settings-nav{position:sticky;top:24px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px}`\n  - Buttons with data-scroll; active.\n- `.settings-content` sections.\n- `.settings-section{margin-bottom:32px;padding-bottom:24px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-2)}`; last no border.\n- `.settings-section h2{font-size:14px;font-weight:650}`; `.section-desc` 11.5.\n- `.settings-row` for fields: label 150px + value/input.\n  - `.field-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:150px minmax(0,1fr);gap:20px;padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-2)}`\n  - `.field-label` 12px ink-2; `.field-help` 10.5.\n  - `.input` style.\n- Account profile row with avatar; not a card, a row.\n- Buttons.\n- Model rows read-only.\n- A2A URL input + copy button.\n- Interface segmented.\n- About.\n- The theme segmented buttons; active.\n- The density segmented.\n- The language select.\n- The `settings-nav` buttons.\n- The settings page header.\n- The sub-nav active account by default; JS scroll spy optional. On click, set active. Fine.\n- At ≤900, the settings grid stacks; the sub-nav becomes horizontal scroll chips; sticky top 0? The page topbar 52; the sub-nav sticky under? Could set `position:static` on mobile and horizontal. Good.\n\n**Page header / action button**:\n- `.btn` styles from v5: `.btn` height 31, etc. On pages, use `.btn` and `.btn-primary`/outline. The `.btn` base has `white-space:nowrap`. Good.\n- The page actions buttons.\n- `.btn-sm` new height 26.\n- `.btn-danger` from v5 (added). Good.\n- `.btn-ghost` may exist in v5 CSS? Let's check. v5 has `.btn`, `.btn-primary`, `.btn-outline`, `.btn-danger`; `.btn-ghost` was in v2's A2A card CSS (maybe still) but not needed. Define in pages CSS:\n  ```css\n  .btn-ghost{background:transparent;border:1px solid transparent;color:var(--ink-2)}\n  .btn-ghost:hover{background:var(--surface-2);color:var(--ink)}\n  ```\n- `.is-danger-text{color:var(--red)}`.\n\n**Page shell CSS**:\n- `.page-main{min-width:0;min-height:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;background:var(--paper);overflow:hidden}`\n- `.page-topbar{display:none}`\n- `.page-scroll{flex:1;overflow-y:auto;min-height:0}`\n- `.page{max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto;padding:34px 40px 64px}`\n- At ≤1280: padding 30 32; at ≤900: 24 20; at ≤760: 20 14.\n- The page topbar mobile:\n  ```css\n  @media(max-width:900px){\n    .page-topbar{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;height:52px;padding:0 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--paper);flex:none}\n    .page-topbar-title{font-size:13px;font-weight:600}\n    .page-topbar .mobile-sidebar-btn{display:grid;margin-right:0}\n    .page{padding:24px 20px 48px}\n  }\n  ```\n  - The `.mobile-sidebar-btn` base is display none, media at ≤900 display grid from v5 CSS. The page topbar is only shown at ≤900. Good.\n  - The sidebar drawer and scrim from v5 CSS still work.\n  - The page topbar is inside `.page-main`, outside `.page-scroll`, so it stays at the top. Good.\n  - The v5 CSS's `.mobile-sidebar-btn` margin-right 8; in the topbar, plus gap 10; fine.\n  - At ≤900, the page topbar shows; the sidebar drawer's scrim covers it when open. The page topbar button opens.\n- On desktop, the page topbar display none. The page main starts at top; the page padding 34.\n- The sidebar is full height; good.\n\n**App grid override**:\n- In the pages file, modify the v5 CSS:\n  - Base `.app` from 3 cols to 2:\n    ```css\n    grid-template-columns:var(--sidebar-w) minmax(0,1fr);\n    ```\n  - Remove/ignore `.app.trace-collapsed` etc. They won't apply (no trace). The `.app.sidebar-collapsed` rule has 3 columns with trace; must change:\n    ```css\n    .app.sidebar-collapsed{grid-template-columns:var(--sidebar-rail) minmax(0,1fr)}\n    .app.sidebar-collapsed.trace-collapsed{...} /* unused */\n    ```\n  - The `.app.trace-collapsed` rules unused; can leave.\n  - The 1180 media `.app` 2 cols; good.\n  - The 900 media 1 col; good.\n  - At >1180, 2 cols. The `.app.sidebar-collapsed` rule later in base with 3 cols would override the base 2 cols; patch it to 2.\n  - The `.app.sidebar-collapsed.trace-collapsed` unused; leave.\n  - The `.app.trace-collapsed` base with 3 cols unused.\n  - The `.trace` element absent; unused.\n- The `--trace-w` unused.\n- The `.page-main` is the second grid child. Good.\n\n**Sidebar HTML adjustments**:\n- Copy v5 sidebar. Change nav:\n  - \"对话\" anchor to ui-v5.html (not active).\n  - \"智能体\" button data-page=\"agents\" class is-active initially.\n  - \"任务\" button data-page=\"tasks\".\n  - \"知识库\" button data-page=\"knowledge\".\n- The current v5 nav \"对话\" is a button is-active. Need replace the nav block entirely.\n- The newSession button: JS could navigate to ui-v5.html. Or make an anchor. Use a button; pages JS click -> `window.location.href='ui-v5.html'`. The sidebar's `sb-new` CSS. Fine.\n- The sessions click -> `window.location.href='ui-v5.html'`. The pages JS.\n- The account menu settings: button data-page=\"settings\"; account button data-page=\"settings\" maybe.\n- The account menu theme toggle.\n- The session menu/dialog not needed; remove from pages file. The v5 sidebar HTML doesn't include them inside; they are after app. When copying, we can delete those blocks.\n- The session count 7.\n- The `3 ONLINE`.\n- The pages file's nav \"智能体\" active; the page router sets.\n- The page title.\n\n**Main/trace replacement**:\n- Replace from `<main class=\"chat\">` to `</main>` with page main; remove the trace `<aside>` from `<!-- ================= TRACE ================= -->` to `</aside>`.\n- The v5 `main` contains chat header/stream/composer. Remove.\n- The v5 trace.\n- The session menu/dialog after app remove.\n- Keep the toast (v5 toast) and maybe the account menu remains in sidebar.\n- The v5 `<script>` replace entirely.\n- The v5 CSS has chat styles unused; okay.\n\n**Icons**: v5 has most; add page-specific icons? \n- Agents: use i-bot, i-plus, i-refresh (not in v5?), i-external, i-shield, i-trash, i-edit, i-check.\n- v5 has i-refresh? Let's check: v4/v5 sprite includes i-refresh? The old v4 had i-refresh? Looking at the sprite list: i-chat, i-stack, i-bot, i-flow, i-db, i-sliders, i-search, i-plus, i-chevron, i-panel, i-panel-left, i-sun, i-moon, i-clip, i-at, i-up, i-check, i-x, i-clock, i-copy, i-shield, i-stop, i-arrow, i-external, i-archive, i-menu, i-more, i-user, i-logout, i-edit, i-trash. No i-refresh. Need add `i-refresh` for health check/refresh. Also i-upload for knowledge upload, i-file for docs maybe, i-key for auth? We can add:\n  - `i-refresh`: `M20 11a8 8 0 1 0-.8 4M20 5v6h-6`\n  - `i-upload`: `M12 15V4M7 9l5-5 5 5M5 20h14` (upload arrow up; but i-up is up arrow; use a tray)\n  - `i-file`: `M14 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8l-5-5Z` + `M14 3v5h5`\n  - `i-key`: `M14 10a4 4 0 1 1-3.5 2.1L4 18.6V21h3v-2h2v-2h2l1.5-1.5`\n  - `i-filter`? no.\n  - `i-arrow` exists.\n- The pages CSS new.\n\n**Data demos**: The pages file needs a `[data-demo]` handler to show toasts. The v5 script has one; include in pages JS.\n- The toast element exists.\n- The theme toggle in account menu.\n- The account menu/ sidebar JS.\n\n**Pages JS**:\n- Theme init/toggle (same).\n- Sidebar/account:\n  - Vars sidebarToggle, mobileSidebarBtn, sidebarScrim, accountBtn, accountMenu, narrowSidebar.\n  - setAccountMenu, setMobileSidebar, setSidebarCollapsed.\n  - Account menu item settings/account trigger page switching; the theme item toggles; other data-demo.\n  - The account menu \"设置\" button with `data-page=\"settings\"`; click -> showPage('settings'). The \"账号\" maybe data-page settings + section account.\n  - The menu item close listener. But if a menu item also triggers page switch, both.\n  - The account menu items are buttons; settings data-page. The click listener `showPage`.\n- Page router:\n  - `var pages = ['agents','tasks','knowledge','settings'];`\n  - `showPage(name, opts)`:\n    - if name not valid, agents.\n    - hide all `.page`; show.\n    - update nav active: `.sb-nav-item[data-page]`; remove active; set for name if in agents/tasks/knowledge.\n    - update topbar title and document.title.\n    - close menu.\n    - scroll top.\n    - `history.replaceState(null,'','#'+name)`.\n    - If settings and section, scroll.\n  - Nav buttons `data-page` click.\n  - Account menu `data-page` click.\n  - On load, parse hash; if `settings` -> settings; if agents/tasks/knowledge -> that; else agents.\n  - The nav \"对话\" is an anchor to ui-v5.html.\n  - The nav active initially set by JS.\n- Session actions in the pages sidebar:\n  - For each `.session`, click -> `window.location.href='ui-v5.html'`.\n  - The newSession click -> ui-v5.html.\n  - No more/delete in pages; the main chat has it.\n- Tasks filter:\n  - `data-filter` buttons; `.task-item[data-state]`; hide.\n  - Active class.\n- Agents filter:\n  - `data-filter` buttons health; agent items data-health; hide.\n  - Search input filter by text.\n  - The \"全部/健康/降级/已禁用\" counts.\n  - The disabled filter no items; show empty? If selected, all hidden; maybe a \"没有匹配项\" row? Not necessary.\n- Register toggle:\n  - `registerAgentBtn` toggles `.register-panel` hidden; update text? Keep.\n  - The cancel? Add a \"取消\" button inside the panel maybe. The panel actions include \"拉取 Agent Card\" and \"注册\"; no cancel. The toggle button can close. Fine.\n- Settings sub-nav:\n  - Buttons `data-scroll`; click scroll to section, set active.\n  - The page is the `page-scroll` container; `document.getElementById(section).scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth', block:'start'})`. The section's top may be under the sticky? The settings page doesn't have a sticky topbar on desktop; the page scroll. Good. On mobile, the page topbar is fixed outside scroll; scrollIntoView start at the top of the scroll container, fine.\n  - The sub-nav sticky; active.\n- Theme controls:\n  - `[data-theme-choice]` buttons; click set theme, localStorage, sync.\n  - `syncThemeControls` sets active based on root.dataset.theme.\n  - The account menu theme toggle calls the same theme toggle and sync.\n  - The theme toggle's icons swap via CSS.\n- Copy A2A URL:\n  - Button `id=copyA2A`; use navigator.clipboard; fallback; toast.\n- Upload/refresh/health/etc. data-demo.\n- The toast.\n- The Esc: close account/mobile.\n- The account menu outside click.\n- The mobile drawer.\n- The sidebar collapse/restore on resize.\n- The page topbar title.\n\n**Page switching nav active**:\n- The sidebar nav \"对话\" is an anchor, not a button; not in `[data-page]`.\n- The nav buttons agents/tasks/knowledge.\n- The settings page no nav active.\n- If settings, remove active from all nav items. Good.\n- The account menu settings click sets page settings; the menu closes.\n- The account button \"账号\" could set page settings and scroll to account. Add data-page settings + data-section account.\n- The mobile drawer closes after page switch.\n\n**Initial page**:\n- The file could open on agents by default. The user can switch. If hash settings, show settings.\n- The nav active set.\n- The page title.\n\n**Title/header**:\n- Each page has its own h1; the document title updates.\n- The topbar title.\n\n**Sidebar session list**:\n- Clicking navigates to chat. The more buttons in the pages file? We remove the v5 session wrap JS; no more buttons. The session list is static; the user can go to chat for actions. Good.\n- But the v5 CSS `.session-row` etc. unused. Fine.\n- The v5 session menu/dialog HTML removed. Good.\n\n**What about the chat page v5's nav links to pages and the pages file's back link**:\n- The pages file's \"对话\" nav anchor to ui-v5.html. Good.\n- The pages file's account settings button. Good.\n- The chat page's settings anchor to pages settings. Good.\n\n**Create pages file via copy v5**:\n- Copy v5 → ui-v5-pages.html.\n- Replace title/comment.\n- Replace main+trace.\n- Replace script.\n- Remove v5 session menu/dialog.\n- Adjust sidebar nav.\n- Patch CSS base app + add page CSS in a second `<style>`.\n- Add icons.\n- Validate.\n\nThis is a lot of HTML for four pages. Let's write it carefully.\n\nFirst, patch the shell CSS base in the pages file:\n- `.app{grid-template-columns:var(--sidebar-w) minmax(0,1fr) var(--trace-w);}` → 2 cols.\n- `.app.sidebar-collapsed{grid-template-columns:var(--sidebar-rail) minmax(0,1fr) var(--trace-w)}` → 2 cols.\n- `.app.trace-collapsed` unused; leave.\n- The 1180 media `.app` 2 cols; good.\n- The 900 media 1 col; good.\n- The `.page-main` new.\n- The v5 CSS `.chat` unused.\n- The `.sidebar` and account menu CSS used.\n- The v5 CSS `.app` at 1280 changes `--sidebar-w` and `--trace-w`; trace unused. Fine.\n- The v5 CSS at 1180 `.app{grid-template-columns:var(--sidebar-w) minmax(0,1fr)}`; good.\n- The v5 CSS at 900 `.app,...{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}`; good.\n- The v5 CSS `.trace` fixed; no element.\n- The `.mobile-sidebar-btn` CSS base display none, at ≤900 display grid; used in page topbar. Good.\n- The `sidebar-scrim` CSS; used.\n- The `.app.sidebar-collapsed` base patched 2 cols. At 1180 media `.app.sidebar-collapsed` 2 cols; good. At 900 media all 1 col.\n- At >1180 with sidebar collapsed, grid 56 + 1fr; good.\n\nPatch the main/trace:\n- Locate `<main class=\"chat\">` ... `</main>` then the trace aside. The v5 includes a comment `<!-- ================= TRACE ================= -->`. The trace is after main. Replace from `<main class=\"chat\">` to the end of trace `</aside>` with the page main.\n- The sidebar remains before.\n- The scrim remains before main.\n- The session menu/dialog after app remove.\n- The toast remains.\n- The script replaced.\n\n**Page main HTML**:\nLet's write the full content. This will be long. I'll compose carefully.\n\n**Agents page**:\n```html\n<section class=\"page\" id=\"page-agents\" data-page=\"agents\">\n  <header class=\"page-head\">\n    <div class=\"page-heading\">\n      <h1 class=\"page-title\">智能体</h1>\n      <p class=\"page-sub\">管理通过 A2A 注册的远程智能体，查看 Agent Card、技能与健康状态。</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"page-actions\">\n      <button class=\"btn btn-outline\" data-demo=\"刷新全部（原型演示）\">刷新</button>\n      <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" id=\"registerAgentBtn\"><svg plus>注册智能体</button>\n    </div>\n  </header>\n\n  <div class=\"stats\">\n    <div class=\"stat\"><span class=\"stat-value\">3</span><span class=\"stat-label\">已注册</span></div>\n    ...\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"register-panel\" id=\"registerPanel\" hidden>\n    ...\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"toolbar\">\n    <div class=\"seg\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"按健康状态筛选\">\n      <button class=\"is-active\" data-agent-filter=\"all\">全部 <span>3</span></button>\n      <button data-agent-filter=\"healthy\">健康 <span>2</span></button>\n      <button data-agent-filter=\"degraded\">降级 <span>1</span></button>\n      <button data-agent-filter=\"disabled\">已禁用 <span>0</span></button>\n    </div>\n    <label class=\"tool-search\">\n      <svg search><input id=\"agentSearch\" placeholder=\"搜索名称或 slug\">\n    </label>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"agent-list\" id=\"agentList\">\n    <details class=\"agent-item\" data-health=\"healthy\" open> ... </details>\n    ...\n  </div>\n</section>\n```\n\n- The register panel:\n```html\n<div class=\"register-panel\" id=\"registerPanel\" hidden>\n  <div class=\"register-grid\">\n    <label class=\"field\"><span>Agent URL</span><input class=\"input\" placeholder=\"https://agent.example.com/a2a\"></label>\n    <label class=\"field\"><span>Slug</span><input class=\"input\" placeholder=\"code-assistant\"></label>\n    <label class=\"field\"><span>鉴权引用</span><input class=\"input\" placeholder=\"env:CODE_AGENT_KEY\"></label>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"register-actions\">\n    <button class=\"btn btn-outline\" data-demo=\"拉取 Agent Card（原型演示）\">拉取 Agent Card</button>\n    <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" id=\"confirmRegister\">确认注册</button>\n    <span class=\"note\">先校验 URL 与 Agent Card，密钥只保存引用。</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n- The `hidden` attr; CSS `.register-panel[hidden]{display:none}`? The global `[hidden]` UA display none; but `.register-panel{display:block}` author style could override. Use `.register-panel[hidden]{display:none}` explicitly.\n- The register toggle JS sets `hidden` false/true.\n- The confirm register closes and toast.\n- The fields class `.field` (new).\n- The `.input`.\n\n- Agent item summary:\n```html\n<details class=\"agent-item\" data-health=\"healthy\" open>\n  <summary class=\"agent-summary\">\n    <span class=\"agent-badge\">DA</span>\n    <span class=\"agent-main\">\n      <span class=\"agent-name\">data-analyst</span>\n      <span class=\"agent-slug\">data-analyst · A2A 1.0</span>\n    </span>\n    <span class=\"agent-endpoint\">https://data.example.com/a2a</span>\n    <span class=\"agent-skill-count\">2 个技能</span>\n    <span class=\"agent-health\"><span class=\"st st-ok\"><span class=\"dot is-ok\"></span>健康</span></span>\n    <svg class=\"ic agent-chev\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-chevron\"/></svg>\n  </summary>\n  <div class=\"agent-detail\">\n    <div class=\"detail-block\">\n      <h4>技能</h4>\n      <div class=\"skill-list\">\n        <span class=\"skill-chip\">verify_numbers</span>\n        <span class=\"skill-chip\">analyze_tickets</span>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"detail-note\">每个技能生成一个工具：<span class=\"mono\">agent_data_analyst__verify_numbers</span></p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"detail-block\">\n      <h4>连接</h4>\n      <dl class=\"kv\">\n        <dt>协议</dt><dd>A2A 1.0 · JSON-RPC</dd>\n        <dt>鉴权</dt><dd><span class=\"mono\">bearer</span> · <span class=\"mono\">env:DATA_AGENT_KEY</span></dd>\n        <dt>最近检查</dt><dd>23:41:08 · 200 OK · 142ms</dd>\n      </dl>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"detail-block wide\">\n      <h4>操作</h4>\n      <div class=\"detail-actions\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-outline btn-sm\" data-demo=\"健康检查（原型演示）\">健康检查</button>\n        <button class=\"btn btn-outline btn-sm\" data-demo=\"刷新 Agent Card（原型演示）\">刷新 Card</button>\n        <button class=\"btn btn-ghost btn-sm\" data-demo=\"禁用智能体（原型演示）\">禁用</button>\n        <button class=\"btn btn-ghost btn-sm is-danger-text\" data-demo=\"删除智能体（原型演示）\">删除</button>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</details>\n```\n- The `.agent-summary` grid.\n- The `.agent-chev` rotate.\n- The `.kv` exists in v5 CSS (global). Good.\n- The `.detail-note`.\n- The actions.\n- The first open.\n- Editorial:\n  - badge ER, name editorial-reviewer, slug, endpoint https://editorial.example.com/a2a, 1 skill, healthy.\n  - Details: review_copy; 连接; actions.\n- Code:\n  - badge CA, code-assistant, https://code.example.com/a2a, 2 skills, degraded.\n  - Details: review_code, explain_code; 连接; 最近检查 23:39:52 · 502 a2a_unavailable (red); actions; maybe \"启用\" already.\n  - data-health=\"degraded\".\n- The stats: 3, 2, 1, 3.\n- The filters: all 3, healthy 2, degraded 1, disabled 0.\n- The code row's health chip `st-warn` \"降级\".\n- The filter JS.\n\n**Tasks page**:\n```html\n<section class=\"page\" id=\"page-tasks\" data-page=\"tasks\" hidden>\n  <header class=\"page-head\">\n    <div class=\"page-heading\">\n      <h1 class=\"page-title\">任务</h1>\n      <p class=\"page-sub\">跟踪主智能体发起的 A2A 任务，查看状态、产出与耗时。</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"page-actions\">\n      <button class=\"btn btn-outline\" data-demo=\"刷新任务（原型演示）\">刷新</button>\n    </div>\n  </header>\n  <div class=\"stats\">4 / 1 运行中 / 2 已完成 / 1 失败</div>\n  <div class=\"toolbar\">\n    <div class=\"seg\" id=\"taskFilters\">\n      <button class=\"is-active\" data-task-filter=\"all\">全部 <span>4</span></button>\n      <button data-task-filter=\"working\">运行中 <span>1</span></button>\n      <button data-task-filter=\"completed\">已完成 <span>2</span></button>\n      <button data-task-filter=\"failed\">失败 <span>1</span></button>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"task-table\">\n    <div class=\"task-head\">\n      <span>任务</span><span>远程智能体</span><span>状态</span><span>耗时</span><span>所属会话</span><span></span>\n    </div>\n    <details class=\"task-item\" data-state=\"working\" open> ... </details>\n    ...\n  </div>\n</section>\n```\n- Task summary:\n```html\n<summary class=\"task-summary\">\n  <span class=\"task-main\"><span class=\"task-id mono\">task_2e91</span><span class=\"task-skill\">review_copy</span></span>\n  <span class=\"task-agent\">editorial-reviewer <small>a2a</small></span>\n  <span><span class=\"st st-live\"><span class=\"dot is-live\"></span>运行中</span></span>\n  <span class=\"task-duration mono\">00:12</span>\n  <span class=\"task-conv\">退款政策变更的影响面</span>\n  <svg class=\"ic task-chev\"><use href=\"#i-chevron\"/></svg>\n</summary>\n```\n- Detail:\n```html\n<div class=\"task-detail\">\n  <div class=\"detail-block\">\n    <h4>请求</h4>\n    <dl class=\"kv\">\n      <dt>技能</dt><dd><span class=\"mono\">agent_editorial_reviewer__review_copy</span></dd>\n      <dt>参数</dt><dd>审阅“退款政策变更说明”的措辞</dd>\n      <dt>Run</dt><dd><span class=\"mono\">run_4c1d_e8</span></dd>\n    </dl>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"detail-block\">\n    <h4>状态时间线</h4>\n    <ol class=\"task-timeline\">\n      <li class=\"is-done\"><span class=\"tl-dot\"></span><div><b>submitted</b><small>23:44:02</small></div></li>\n      <li class=\"is-now\"><span class=\"tl-dot\"></span><div><b>working</b><small>23:44:03 · 已运行 12s</small></div></li>\n      <li><span class=\"tl-dot\"></span><div><b>completed</b><small>等待中</small></div></li>\n    </ol>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"detail-block wide\">\n    <h4>产出</h4>\n    <p class=\"detail-note\">尚未产出。任务完成后会写入 artifact，并更新所属会话。</p>\n    <div class=\"detail-actions\">\n      <button class=\"btn btn-outline btn-sm is-danger-text\" data-demo=\"取消任务（原型演示）\">取消任务</button>\n      <a class=\"btn btn-ghost btn-sm\" href=\"ui-v5.html\">打开会话</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n- The `.task-timeline` CSS.\n- Completed rows:\n  - task_7c1e editorial-reviewer review_copy completed 1.8s Q3 客服工单周报.\n  - Details: artifact \"3 处措辞建议\"; timeline submitted/working/completed; action 打开会话.\n  - task_9b2a data-analyst verify_numbers completed 1.2s Q3...; artifact \"12/12 项数字核对通过\".\n  - failed task_1a77 code-assistant review_code failed 6.4s 审查...; error \"502 a2a_unavailable · 远程 Agent 在 60s 内未响应\"; action 打开会话.\n- The table head spans.\n- The filters hide.\n- The first working open.\n\n**Knowledge page**:\n```html\n<section class=\"page\" id=\"page-knowledge\" data-page=\"knowledge\" hidden>\n  <header class=\"page-head\">\n    <div class=\"page-heading\">\n      <h1 class=\"page-title\">知识库</h1>\n      <p class=\"page-sub\">support-kb · pgvector HNSW · cosine · 128 篇文档。</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"page-actions\">\n      <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" data-demo=\"上传文档（原型演示）\"><svg upload>上传文档</button>\n    </div>\n  </header>\n  <div class=\"stats\">... 128 文档 / 1,842 片段 / 124 就绪 / 1 失败</div>\n  <div class=\"knowledge-grid\">\n    <section class=\"panel doc-panel\">\n      <div class=\"panel-head\">\n        <h2>文档</h2><span class=\"count\">5 / 128</span>\n        <span class=\"spacer\"></span>\n        <button class=\"text-link\" data-demo=\"查看全部文档（原型演示）\">查看全部</button>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"doc-toolbar\">\n        <label class=\"tool-search\"><svg search><input placeholder=\"搜索文档\"></label>\n        <select class=\"select\"><option>全部分类</option>...</select>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"doc-list\">\n        ... rows ...\n      </div>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"panel debug-panel\">\n      <div class=\"panel-head\"><h2>检索调试</h2><span class=\"tag\">vector search</span></div>\n      <p class=\"panel-desc\">直接调用 <span class=\"mono\">POST /knowledge/search</span>，验证召回与相似度。</p>\n      <div class=\"debug-form\">\n        <label class=\"field\"><span>查询</span><input class=\"input\" value=\"退款需要保留吊牌吗\"></label>\n        <div class=\"debug-row\">\n          <label class=\"field\"><span>top_k</span><select class=\"select\"><option>5</option><option>10</option></select></label>\n          <label class=\"field\"><span>分类</span><select class=\"select\"><option>售后</option>...</select></label>\n          <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" data-demo=\"执行检索（原型演示）\">检索</button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"debug-results\">\n        <div class=\"result\">\n          <div class=\"result-top\"><span class=\"result-title\">退款政策</span><span class=\"result-score\">0.83</span></div>\n          <div class=\"result-src\">chunk_51de · 退款政策.md · 32ms</div>\n          <p class=\"result-excerpt\">退货需要保留吊牌与包装，签收后 7 天内可申请…</p>\n        </div>\n        ...\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"debug-meta\">42ms · top_k=5 · cosine</div>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n</section>\n```\n- Document rows:\n  - Q3 客服复盘 v2 · 客服 · 24 chunks · 09-30 · ready\n  - 工单分类规范 v3 · 客服 · 12 chunks · 09-18 · ready\n  - 退款处理 SOP · 客服 · 18 chunks · 08-02 · ready\n  - 售后话术库 · 客服 · indexing · 07-21 · indexing\n  - 产品发布说明 Q3 · 产品 · failed · 07-15\n- Use `.doc-row` with a status dot and title/meta; status chip.\n- The left panel's count \"5 / 128\".\n- The right panel results.\n- The `tool-search` class; `.select`; `.field`.\n- The page stats.\n\n**Settings page**:\n```html\n<section class=\"page page-settings\" id=\"page-settings\" data-page=\"settings\" hidden>\n  <header class=\"page-head\">\n    <div><h1>设置</h1><p>账号、模型、A2A 端点与界面偏好。</p></div>\n  </header>\n  <div class=\"settings-grid\">\n    <nav class=\"settings-nav\" aria-label=\"设置分区\">\n      <button class=\"settings-nav-item is-active\" data-scroll=\"settings-account\">账号</button>\n      ...\n    </nav>\n    <div class=\"settings-content\">\n      <section class=\"settings-section\" id=\"settings-account\">\n        <div class=\"section-head\"><h2>账号</h2><p>...</p></div>\n        <div class=\"profile-row\">avatar + name/email</div>\n        <div class=\"field-row\">展示名 input</div>\n        <div class=\"field-row\">邮箱 input readonly</div>\n        <div class=\"settings-actions\"><button>修改密码</button><button>退出登录</button></div>\n      </section>\n      ...\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n```\n- Sub-nav buttons.\n- Account.\n- Model section with `.kv` read-only rows.\n- A2A section with URL input + copy button; auth rows.\n- Interface section with theme segmented (`data-theme-choice`), language select, density segmented.\n- About section.\n- The theme control.\n- The copy button.\n- The page settings uses `.page-settings` maybe max width 980.\n- The sub-nav sticky.\n- The sections.\n\n**CSS additions**:\nAdd a second `<style>` after the v5 style? The v5 `</style>` is before the icon sprite. We can insert a second `<style>` right after the first `</style>`. The page CSS:\n- Override `.app`? We'll patch the v5 CSS base instead.\n- Add page styles.\n- Add responsive page styles.\n- Maybe override `.trace`/`.chat` unused.\n- The page CSS should use the same tokens.\n\nLet's write the page CSS:\n\n```css\n/* page shell */\n.page-main{...}\n.page-topbar{...}\n.page-scroll{...}\n.page{...}\n.page[hidden]{display:none}\n.page-head{...}\n.page-heading{...}\n.page-title{...}\n.page-sub{...}\n.page-actions{...}\n.btn-sm{...}\n.btn-ghost{...}\n.is-danger-text{...}\n.stats{...}\n.stat{...}\n.stat-value{...}\n.stat-label{...}\n.toolbar{...}\n.seg{...}\n.seg button{...}\n.seg button.is-active{...}\n.seg button span{...}\n.tool-search{...}\n.tool-search .ic{...}\n.tool-search input{...}\n.input,.select{...}\n.field{...}\n.field > span{...}\n.note{...}\n.st{...}\n.st-ok{...}\n.st-warn{...}\n.st-error{...}\n.st-muted{...}\n.st-live{...}\n.st .dot{...}\n```\n- The `.st` chips:\n```css\n.st{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:5px;height:22px;padding:0 7px;border:1px solid transparent;border-radius:4px;font-size:10.5px;font-weight:500;white-space:nowrap}\n.st .dot{width:5px;height:5px}\n.st-ok{background:var(--green-soft);color:var(--green)}\n.st-warn{background:var(--amber-soft);color:var(--amber-text)}\n.st-error{background:var(--red-soft);color:var(--red)}\n.st-muted{background:var(--surface-2);color:var(--ink-3);border-color:var(--line-2)}\n.st-live{background:var(--amber-soft);color:var(--amber-text)}\n```\n- The `.dot` colors: `.st-ok .dot{background:var(--green)}` etc. The existing `.dot.is-ok` can be used inside; define.\n- Agents:\n```css\n.agent-list{border-top:1px solid var(--line)}\n.agent-item{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}\n.agent-summary{display:grid;grid-template-columns:30px minmax(0,1.1fr) minmax(0,1fr) 64px 80px 16px;gap:16px;align-items:center;padding:14px 4px;cursor:pointer;list-style:none}\n...\n```\n- The summary's first column badge; the agent main; endpoint; skills; health; chevron. 6 columns. Good.\n- The `.agent-item[open] .agent-chev{transform:rotate(180deg)}`.\n- `.agent-detail{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px 32px;padding:2px 4px 18px 46px}`.\n- `.detail-block h4{font-size:10.5px;color:var(--ink-3);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.03em;margin-bottom:7px}`.\n- `.skill-chip` etc.\n- `.detail-actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px}`.\n- `.detail-note{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ink-3);line-height:1.6}`.\n- The `.kv` from v5: `display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr`; good. But `.kv` in v5 is used in MCP card; the page uses it. Good. It has `margin-top:9px`; maybe adjust; fine.\n- The agent detail's `.kv` dt/dd. Good.\n- The `.agent-endpoint` ellipsis.\n- The `.agent-skill-count` font 10.5 mono? Use 11.\n- The `.agent-health` justify-self end.\n- The `.agent-chev` transition.\n\n- Tasks:\n```css\n.task-table{border-top:1px solid var(--line)}\n.task-head,.task-summary{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.1fr) minmax(0,1fr) 90px 64px minmax(0,1.2fr) 16px;gap:16px;align-items:center}\n.task-head{padding:9px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-size:10.5px;color:var(--ink-3);letter-spacing:.02em}\n.task-item{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}\n.task-summary{padding:12px 4px;cursor:pointer;list-style:none}\n.task-summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}\n.task-main{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;min-width:0}\n.task-id{font-size:11px;color:var(--ink-3)}\n.task-skill{font-size:12px;font-weight:550;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}\n.task-agent{font-size:12px;color:var(--ink-2)}\n.task-agent small{font-family:mono;font-size:9px;color:var(--ink-3)}\n.task-duration{font-size:11px;color:var(--ink-2)}\n.task-conv{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ink-3);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}\n.task-chev{...}\n.task-item[open] .task-chev{transform:rotate(180deg)}\n.task-detail{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:18px 32px;padding:4px 4px 18px}\n.task-timeline{...}\n.task-timeline li{position:relative;padding:0 0 14px 18px;border-left:1px solid var(--line-2);margin-left:4px}\n.task-timeline li:last-child{border-left-color:transparent}\n.tl-dot{position:absolute;left:-4px;top:3px;width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--surface);border:1.5px solid var(--line)}\n.is-done .tl-dot{background:var(--green);border-color:var(--green)}\n.is-now .tl-dot{background:var(--amber);border-color:var(--amber)}\n...\n```\n- The task detail grid 2 columns; the actions wide.\n- The `.task-detail .detail-block` etc.\n- The filter hides items.\n\n- Knowledge:\n```css\n.knowledge-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.5fr) minmax(320px,.9fr);gap:28px;align-items:start}\n.panel{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:var(--surface);overflow:hidden}\n.panel-head{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:13px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-2)}\n.panel-head h2{font-size:13px;font-weight:650}\n.panel-head .count{font-family:mono;font-size:10px;color:var(--ink-3)}\n.panel-head .spacer{flex:1}\n.panel-desc{padding:12px 16px 0;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ink-3);line-height:1.6}\n.doc-toolbar{display:flex;gap:8px;padding:10px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-2)}\n.doc-toolbar .tool-search{flex:1}\n.doc-list{padding:0 12px}\n.doc-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:11px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-2)}\n.doc-row:last-child{border-bottom:0}\n.doc-main{flex:1;min-width:0}\n.doc-title{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:550;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}\n.doc-meta{margin-top:2px;font-size:10px;color:var(--ink-3)}\n.doc-status{flex:none}\n.panel-foot{padding:10px 16px;border-top:1px solid var(--line-2);font-size:10.5px;color:var(--ink-3)}\n.debug-panel{position:sticky;top:24px}\n.debug-form{padding:12px 16px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px}\n.debug-form .field...; .debug-row{display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:flex-end}\n.debug-row .field{flex:1}\n.debug-results{padding:0 16px}\n.result{padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-2)}\n.result-top{display:flex;...}\n.result-title{...}\n.result-score{font-family:mono;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--prussian)}\n.result-src{...}\n.result-excerpt{...}\n.debug-meta{padding:10px 16px;border-top:...;font-family:mono;font-size:9.5px;color:var(--ink-3)}\n```\n- The `.panel-head .tag` uses the existing `.tag` style (small mono border). Good.\n- The `.debug-panel` sticky; the page scroll. Good.\n- The `.doc-toolbar .select` width auto.\n- The `tool-search` component.\n- The `.field` for the debug form; the `.field > span` label; input.\n- The search button in `.debug-row`; align-end.\n\n- Settings:\n```css\n.settings-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:150px minmax(0,1fr);gap:32px;align-items:start}\n.settings-nav{position:sticky;top:24px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px}\n.settings-nav-item{display:flex;align-items:center;height:30px;padding:0 9px;border-radius:5px;font-size:12px;color:var(--ink-3);text-align:left}\n.settings-nav-item:hover{background:var(--surface-2);color:var(--ink)}\n.settings-nav-item.is-active{background:var(--surface);color:var(--ink);font-weight:600;box-shadow:var(--shadow-sm)}\n.settings-content{min-width:0}\n.settings-section{padding-bottom:24px;margin-bottom:28px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-2);scroll-margin-top:24px}\n.settings-section:last-child{border-bottom:0}\n.section-head h2{font-size:14px;font-weight:650}\n.section-head p{margin-top:4px;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--ink-3)}\n.profile-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:14px 0}\n.profile-row .avatar{width:40px;height:40px;font-size:14px}\n.profile-name{font-size:13px;font-weight:600}\n.profile-email{font-size:11px;color:var(--ink-3);margin-top:2px}\n.field-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:150px minmax(0,1fr);gap:20px;align-items:center;padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-2)}\n.field-label{font-size:12px;color:var(--ink-2)}\n.field-label small{display:block;margin-top:2px;font-size:10px;color:var(--ink-3)}\n.field-row .input{max-width:360px}\n.settings-actions{display:flex;gap:8px;margin-top:14px}\n.settings-kv{...}\n.theme-seg{...}\n...\n```\n- The `.avatar` exists in v5.\n- The `.input` global page style.\n- The `.select`.\n- The `.settings-nav` sticky; the page scroll.\n- The `.settings-section` scroll-margin-top.\n- The `.theme-seg` uses `.seg`.\n- The `.density-seg`.\n- The `.settings-actions`.\n- The `.about-list`.\n- The `.link` style.\n- The `.note` style.\n\n- Page responsive:\n```css\n@media (max-width:1180px){\n  .page{padding:30px 32px 56px}\n}\n@media (max-width:900px){\n  .page-main{...}\n  .page-topbar{display:flex;...}\n  .page{padding:24px 20px 48px}\n  .knowledge-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}\n  .debug-panel{position:static}\n  .settings-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}\n  .settings-nav{position:static;flex-direction:row;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px}\n  .settings-nav-item{height:28px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--surface)}\n  .settings-nav-item.is-active{...}\n  .agent-summary{grid-template-columns:30px minmax(0,1fr) 80px 16px}\n  .agent-endpoint,.agent-skill-count{display:none}\n  .agent-head? ... \n  .task-head{display:none}\n  .task-summary{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 80px 16px;gap:10px}\n  .task-agent,.task-duration{display:none}\n  .task-detail{grid-template-columns:1fr}\n  .page-actions{...}\n}\n@media (max-width:760px){\n  .page{padding:20px 14px 44px}\n  .page-head{flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:14px}\n  .page-actions{width:100%}\n  .page-title{font-size:22px}\n  .stats{flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0 20px}\n  .stat{border-right:0;margin-right:0;padding-right:0}\n  .toolbar{flex-direction:column;align-items:stretch}\n  .seg{overflow-x:auto}\n  .field-row{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:4px}\n  .settings-actions{flex-wrap:wrap}\n  .agent-detail{padding-left:4px;grid-template-columns:1fr}\n  .detail-block.wide{...}\n  .register-panel...\n  .debug-row{flex-wrap:wrap}\n}\n```\n- The agent summary at 900 hides endpoint/skills; at 760 the health chip maybe; keep.\n- The task summary at 900 hides agent/duration; the task id/skill, status, conversation, chevron. The grid columns 3; but the header hidden. The summary has 6 children; hiding agent/duration leaves task-main, status, conv, chev. Good.\n- The task detail grid stacks.\n- The settings nav horizontal.\n- The page topbar.\n\n**JS pages**:\nWrite from scratch, reusing sidebar/account logic:\n```js\n(function(){\n  var root=...; var app=...;\n  var toast=...; var toastText=...;\n  var sidebarToggle=...; var mobileSidebarBtn=...; var sidebarScrim=...; var accountBtn=...; var accountMenu=...;\n  var narrowSidebar=...;\n  var pageScroll=document.getElementById('pageScroll');\n  var mobilePageTitle=...;\n  var currentPage='agents';\n  // theme init\n  // showToast\n  // account menu functions\n  // sidebar functions\n  // page router\n  // nav buttons\n  // account menu data-page\n  // session list click -> ui-v5.html\n  // newSession click -> ui-v5.html\n  // tasks filter\n  // agents filter/search\n  // register toggle\n  // settings nav scroll\n  // theme controls\n  // copy A2A\n  // data-demo\n  // Esc\n  // initial showPage from hash\n})();\n```\n- The account menu theme toggle `id=themeToggle`; bind theme toggle. It is inside the menu; the menu item close listener will close. Add `syncThemeControls`.\n- The page router:\n```js\n  var pageNames = ['agents','tasks','knowledge','settings'];\n  function showPage(name, section) {\n    if (pageNames.indexOf(name) === -1) name='agents';\n    currentPage=name;\n    document.querySelectorAll('.page').forEach(function(p){ p.hidden = p.getAttribute('data-page') !== name; });\n    document.querySelectorAll('.sb-nav-item[data-page]').forEach(function(n){ n.classList.toggle('is-active', n.getAttribute('data-page')===name); n.removeAttribute('aria-current'); if (...) n.setAttribute('aria-current','page'); });\n    document.querySelectorAll('.account-menu .menu-item[data-page]')....? no persistent active.\n    var titles={agents:'智能体',tasks:'任务',knowledge:'知识库',settings:'设置'};\n    mobilePageTitle.textContent=titles[name];\n    document.title=titles[name]+' · Agent Hub';\n    pageScroll.scrollTop=0;\n    history.replaceState(null,'','#'+name);\n    setAccountMenu(false);\n    if (narrowSidebar.matches) setMobileSidebar(false);\n    if (section) { ... scroll ... }\n  }\n  document.querySelectorAll('.sb-nav-item[data-page]').forEach(btn=>btn.addEventListener('click', ()=>showPage(btn.getAttribute('data-page'))));\n  document.querySelectorAll('[data-page].menu-item') ... for settings/account. But these are in the account menu; if we add listeners, the menu item close listeners also. Use `document.querySelectorAll('[data-page]')` excluding nav? Could bind all elements with data-page; the nav buttons and menu items. But the menu item for settings has data-page; the listener. The menu item close listener (from account menu code) also closes. Fine.\n```\n- The nav buttons `data-page` and the account menu `data-page` both use the same; bind `document.querySelectorAll('[data-page]')` and skip elements inside `.page`? The page sections have `data-page` attributes! The `.page` sections have data-page; binding them would be wrong. Use `.sb-nav-item[data-page], .account-menu .menu-item[data-page]`.\n- The account menu \"账号\" `data-page=\"settings\" data-section=\"account\"`.\n- The settings nav scroll:\n```js\n  function scrollToSection(id){\n    var el=document.getElementById(id); if(!el) return;\n    el.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth', block:'start'});\n    settingsNavItems.forEach(... active based on data-scroll===id);\n  }\n```\n- The page scroll container is `.page-scroll`; scrollIntoView works.\n- The settings sub-nav buttons `data-scroll`.\n- The theme controls:\n```js\n  function applyTheme(theme){\n    root.dataset.theme=theme;\n    try{localStorage.setItem('ah-theme',theme)}catch(e){}\n    syncThemeControls();\n  }\n  function syncThemeControls(){\n    document.querySelectorAll('[data-theme-choice]').forEach(function(b){ b.classList.toggle('is-active', b.getAttribute('data-theme-choice')===root.dataset.theme); });\n  }\n```\n- The account menu theme toggle:\n```js\n  document.getElementById('themeToggle').addEventListener('click', function(){\n    applyTheme(root.dataset.theme==='dark'?'light':'dark');\n    showToast(...);\n  });\n```\n- The theme choice buttons.\n- The initial theme from localStorage.\n- The page load showPage from hash; if hash starts with `settings`, settings; if `agents` etc.\n- The nav active; the account menu.\n- The tasks filter:\n```js\n  document.querySelectorAll('[data-task-filter]').forEach(function(btn){\n    btn.addEventListener('click', function(){\n      var f=btn.getAttribute('data-task-filter');\n      document.querySelectorAll('[data-task-filter]').forEach(b=>b.classList.toggle('is-active',b===btn));\n      document.querySelectorAll('.task-item').forEach(function(item){ item.hidden = f!=='all' && item.getAttribute('data-state')!==f; });\n    });\n  });\n```\n- The task items have `data-state`; the `.task-head` remains. When all hidden, the table shows header only; okay.\n- The agents filter:\n```js\n  var agentFilter='all';\n  var agentSearch='';\n  function filterAgents(){\n    document.querySelectorAll('.agent-item').forEach(function(item){\n      var health=item.getAttribute('data-health');\n      var text=item.textContent.toLowerCase();\n      var match = (agentFilter==='all' || health===agentFilter) && (agentSearch===''||text.indexOf(agentSearch)!==-1);\n      item.hidden=!match;\n    });\n  }\n  document.querySelectorAll('[data-agent-filter]')...\n  agentSearch input...\n```\n- The code-assistant `data-health=\"degraded\"`, the disabled filter has none.\n- The stats static.\n- The register toggle:\n```js\n  var registerPanel=...; var registerBtn=...\n  registerBtn.addEventListener('click', function(){ registerPanel.hidden=!registerPanel.hidden; });\n  var confirmRegister=...; if(confirmRegister) addEventListener click -> registerPanel.hidden=true; showToast('注册请求已提交（原型）');\n```\n- The \"data-demo\" handler.\n- The copy A2A:\n```js\n  var copyA2A=...; copyA2A.addEventListener('click', function(){ copyText('http://localhost:8000/a2a'); });\n```\n- Use the fallback copy function from v5? The v5 script has `fallbackCopy`/copy-btn logic; we can reuse a simpler copy function.\n- The sidebar/account code same as v5, minus session menu.\n- The session list click -> `window.location.href='ui-v5.html'`; but this leaves the sample. The user may click a session to return to chat. Good.\n- The newSession click -> `window.location.href='ui-v5.html'`.\n- The \"对话\" nav anchor already.\n- The account menu settings/account page switch.\n- The mobile drawer.\n- The page topbar.\n- The account menu theme toggle.\n- The data-demo.\n- The Esc.\n- The initial.\n\n- The page topbar title; the page header h1. Good.\n- The page topbar is hidden desktop; at mobile shown. The mobile button opens sidebar.\n- The page router sets `mobilePageTitle`.\n\n- The sidebar nav \"智能体\" active initially; the page router sets. The initial HTML can have no active or agents active. Set agents active in HTML; JS sets.\n- The \"对话\" anchor not active.\n- The settings page no nav active.\n\n**Sidebar nav HTML in pages file**:\nReplace the nav block from v5:\n```html\n<nav class=\"sb-nav\" aria-label=\"主导航\">\n  <a class=\"sb-nav-item\" href=\"ui-v5.html\" aria-label=\"对话\" title=\"对话\">...对话</a>\n  <button class=\"sb-nav-item is-active\" data-page=\"agents\" aria-current=\"page\" ...>...智能体</button>\n  <button class=\"sb-nav-item\" data-page=\"tasks\"...>任务</button>\n  <button class=\"sb-nav-item\" data-page=\"knowledge\"...>知识库</button>\n</nav>\n```\n- The v5 nav block has the active \"对话\" button and anchors for the pages. Replace.\n- The `.sb-nav-item` active for agents initially.\n\n**Account menu HTML**:\n- The \"账号\" button: `data-page=\"settings\" data-section=\"account\"`; but the JS binding for account menu data-page; fine.\n- The \"设置\" button: `data-page=\"settings\"`.\n- The theme button id.\n- The logout data-demo.\n- The menu close listeners (account menu code) attach to `.menu-item`; the data-page elements also. Good.\n- When clicking settings, the menu close and page switch. The data-page listener also closes mobile drawer via showPage? showPage calls setMobileSidebar(false) if narrow. Good.\n- The account menu is in the sidebar; the page switch.\n\n**Sessions in pages**:\n- The sidebar session list; clicking -> chat. The pages JS:\n```js\ndocument.querySelectorAll('.session').forEach(function(item){ item.addEventListener('click', function(){ window.location.href='ui-v5.html'; }); });\n```\n- No more buttons. The `.session` padding-right 30 from v5? The v5 CSS `.session-row .session` only if wrapped; the pages file won't wrap, so no extra padding. Fine.\n- The session count 7.\n- The session menu/dialog removed from the pages file? If we copy v5 and don't remove, the elements exist but no JS; they are hidden. Harmless. But the session more buttons are not generated (the pages JS doesn't wrap), so the menu never opens. The dialog hidden. We can remove them to keep the file clean. Or keep; no harm. Remove the session menu/dialog markup to reduce. The CSS unused. Fine.\n- If the pages JS includes no session menu, the elements hidden. Remove.\n\n**The pages file's chat CSS** unused; acceptable. The page styles second style block.\n\n**Title**: \"Agent Hub · 页面样例（智能体 / 任务 / 知识库 / 设置）\".\n\n**File size**: ~130K. Fine.\n\nLet's implement step by step:\n\n1. Copy v5 to pages.\n2. Patch title, app grid CSS base.\n3. Replace nav, account menu items.\n4. Remove session menu/dialog.\n5. Replace main+trace with page main.\n6. Add icons (`i-refresh`, `i-upload`, `i-file`).\n7. Add second style block with page CSS.\n8. Replace script.\n9. Validate.\n\nThis is a lot of HTML. Let's write the page main in one big string.\n\nBefore writing, inspect the v5 main/trace boundaries:\n- `<main class=\"chat\">` ...\n- `</main>` then `<!-- ================= TRACE ================= -->` ... `</aside>`.\n- The trace ends before `</div>` (app close). The app close is after trace. The scrim is before main.\n- Replace from `<main class=\"chat\">` to the trace `</aside>` inclusive with page main.\n- The session menu/dialog are after the app close, before toast; remove.\n- The pages main uses the page-topbar and page-scroll.\n- The toast remains.\n\nLet's write the page content. This will be ~700 lines. Need care with tags.\n\nFirst, patch shell/nav/remove menus, then insert page main, then CSS, then JS.\n\nLet's start with copying and shell patches."},{"type":"text","text":"现在生成四个页面的样例文件，共用 v5 的侧栏与账号菜单。"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_nKFNJnbsNJDNRdqMhwJW7180","name":"bash","arguments":"{\"command\": \"cd /home/zhaodan/work/NodeJsProjects/agent-hub-web/docs/prototypes && cp ui-v5.html ui-v5-pages.html && python3 - <<'PY'\\npath='ui-v5-pages.html'\\ns=open(path,encoding='utf-8').read()\\n\\ndef rep(old,new,count=1):\\n    global s\\n    assert old in s, 'MISSING: '+old[:120]\\n    s=s.replace(old,new,count)\\n\\nrep('<title>Agent Hub · 对话工作台（原型 v5）</title>','<title>Agent Hub · 页面样例（智能体 / 任务 / 知识库 / 设置）</title>')\\nrep('Agent Hub UI prototype v5 — \\\"Dispatch Desk\\\"','Agent Hub UI prototype v5 — other pages')\\n\\n# 2-column shell (no chat trace panel)\\nrep('grid-template-columns:var(--sidebar-w) minmax(0,1fr) var(--trace-w);',\\n    'grid-template-columns:var(--sidebar-w) minmax(0,1fr);')\\nrep('.app.sidebar-collapsed{grid-template-columns:var(--sidebar-rail) minmax(0,1fr) var(--trace-w)}',\\n    '.app.sidebar-collapsed{grid-template-columns:var(--sidebar-rail) minmax(0,1fr)}')\\n\\n# nav: chat links back, other pages become buttons\\nold_nav = s[s.index('    <nav class=\\\"sb-nav\\\"'):s.index('    </nav>', s.index('    <nav class=\\\"sb-nav\\\"'))+len('    </nav>')]\\nnew_nav = '''    <nav class=\\\"sb-nav\\\" aria-label=\\\"主导航\\\">\\n      <a class=\\\"sb-nav-item\\\" href=\\\"ui-v5.html\\\" aria-label=\\\"对话\\\" title=\\\"对话\\\">\\n        <svg class=\\\"ic\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"><use href=\\\"#i-chat\\\"/></svg><span>对话</span>\\n      </a>\\n      <button class=\\\"sb-nav-item is-active\\\" data-page=\\\"agents\\\" aria-current=\\\"page\\\" aria-label=\\\"智能体\\\" title=\\\"智能体\\\">\\n        <svg class=\\\"ic\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"><use href=\\\"#i-bot\\\"/></svg><span>智能体</span>\\n      </button>\\n      <button class=\\\"sb-nav-item\\\" data-page=\\\"tasks\\\" aria-label=\\\"任务\\\" title=\\\"任务\\\">\\n        <svg class=\\\"ic\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"><use href=\\\"#i-flow\\\"/></svg><span>任务</span>\\n      </button>\\n      <button class=\\\"sb-nav-item\\\" data-page=\\\"knowledge\\\" aria-label=\\\"知识库\\\" title=\\\"知识库\\\">\\n        <svg class=\\\"ic\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"><use href=\\\"#i-db\\\"/></svg><span>知识库</span>\\n      </button>\\n    </nav>'''\\ns=s.replace(old_nav,new_nav,1)\\n\\n# account menu: account / settings open the settings sample\\nrep('''<button class=\\\"menu-item\\\" role=\\\"menuitem\\\" data-demo=\\\"账号资料（原型演示）\\\">\\n        <svg class=\\\"ic\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"><use href=\\\"#i-user\\\"/></svg>账号\\n      </button>''',\\n'''<button class=\\\"menu-item\\\" role=\\\"menuitem\\\" data-page=\\\"settings\\\" data-section=\\\"account\\\">\\n        <svg class=\\\"ic\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"><use href=\\\"#i-user\\\"/></svg>账号\\n      </button>''')\\nrep('''<a class=\\\"menu-item\\\" role=\\\"menuitem\\\" href=\\\"ui-v5-pages.html#settings\\\">\\n        <svg class=\\\"ic\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"><use href=\\\"#i-sliders\\\"/></svg>设置\\n      </a>''',\\n'''<button class=\\\"menu-item\\\" role=\\\"menuitem\\\" data-page=\\\"settings\\\">\\n        <svg class=\\\"ic\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"><use href=\\\"#i-sliders\\\"/></svg>设置\\n      </button>''')\\n\\n# remove chat-only session menu/dialog (samples don't implement delete here)\\nstart=s.index('<div class=\\\"session-menu\\\" id=\\\"sessionMenu\\\"')\\nend=s.index('<div class=\\\"toast\\\" id=\\\"toast\\\"', start)\\ns=s[:start]+s[end:]\\n\\nopen(path,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\\nprint('pages shell/nav patched')\\nPY\", \"description\": \"Prepare pages file shell and navigation\"}"}],"source":{"kind":"model","provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-flash","replayState":{"response":{"kind":"deepseek-messages","version":1,"model":"deepseek-flash"},"blocks":[{"type":"reasoning","signature":"6e45b238-1ce6-49fb-9c21-f258e5cafc43"},{"type":"text"},{"type":"tool-call"}]}},"id":"6f7ba17c-f8df-4d9d-bbaa-83f36771be65"},"usage":{"inputTokens":226,"outputTokens":24029,"cacheReadTokens":463104,"cacheWriteTokens":0,